WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
FOR ENGLISH SOUNDTRACK ONLY

2
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.720
Τokuma Shoten, Nippon Τelevision,
Hakuhodo & Studio Ghibli present

3
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:35.620
WHISPER OF ΤHE HEARΤ

4
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.380
Shizuku Υoko Honna:
Brittany Snow

5
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.800
Shizuku's Father:
James Sikking

6
00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.120
Shizuku's Mother:
Jean Smart

7
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.230
Baron:
Cary Elwes

8
00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:11.280
‘World Emporium’ Proprietor:
Harold Gould

9
00:01:14.084 --> 00:01:16.678
[Bell dinging]

10
00:01:29.134 --> 00:01:31.193
[People chattering]

11
00:01:48.356 --> 00:01:50.551
[Chattering]

12
00:01:52.327 --> 00:01:55.263
- Hey.
- Hey.

13
00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:03.468
- Good evening.
- Oh, hi, Shizuku.

14
00:02:08.012 --> 00:02:09.411
I'm back.

15
00:02:12.518 --> 00:02:13.883
Oh, hi, honey.

16
00:02:13.952 --> 00:02:17.149
You got a plastic bag
for just one carton of milk?

17
00:02:17.222 --> 00:02:19.019
What? They just give it to you.

18
00:02:19.092 --> 00:02:21.117
[Mom] You could say
you don't need it.

19
00:02:21.194 --> 00:02:22.559
Oh, pour me some of that too.

20
00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:24.824
Dad, I got ice tea.
Do you want some?

21
00:02:24.898 --> 00:02:26.161
Ah, sounds good.

22
00:02:26.233 --> 00:02:27.996
I'll have it at the table.

23
00:02:28.602 --> 00:02:31.901
- Thanks. Done with the computer?
- I'm printing out now.

24
00:02:32.974 --> 00:02:35.499
Maybe we should buy another laptop.

25
00:02:35.577 --> 00:02:38.637
[Groaning] Smells like
cigarettes in here.

26
00:02:38.713 --> 00:02:41.649
Shizuku, you should have
gone to Kashiwazaki too.

27
00:02:41.717 --> 00:02:44.345
No, I didn't want to.
Shiho wears me out.

28
00:02:45.354 --> 00:02:47.380
Oh, by the way,
I have to work tomorrow.

29
00:02:47.457 --> 00:02:50.585
- Do you want me to fix you a lunch?
- That's OK. I'll eat out.

30
00:02:50.661 --> 00:02:54.758
The library's computerizing everything.
Everybody's going crazy at work.

31
00:02:54.833 --> 00:02:58.702
I don't think they should, Dad.
Card catalogs are much better.

32
00:02:58.771 --> 00:03:00.238
Yeah. I like 'em better too.

33
00:03:00.306 --> 00:03:03.298
[Mom] I think you've got
a problem with your report.

34
00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:06.174
- What's the problem?
- Isn't there a line missing here?

35
00:03:06.246 --> 00:03:07.611
[Dad] You're right. Darn.

36
00:03:07.681 --> 00:03:09.876
I'll have to print
the entire thing over.

37
00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.045
[Mom] Can't I use the printer first?
My professor will kill me

38
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.384
if I don't have his paper
turned in tomorrow.

39
00:03:15.456 --> 00:03:17.617
[Shizuku] Seiji Amasawa.

40
00:03:17.692 --> 00:03:19.684
Here he is again.

41
00:03:20.696 --> 00:03:23.893
Shizuku, time to put
the books away and go to bed.

42
00:03:23.966 --> 00:03:25.628
OK, Dad. Good night.

43
00:03:33.577 --> 00:03:36.842
Yep. I knew I had
seen that name before.

44
00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:40.647
[Gasping] Here it is again.

45
00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:42.579
And again.

46
00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:45.021
Seiji Amasawa.

47
00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.649
Seiji Amasawa.

48
00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:49.388
Seiji Amasawa. That's amazing.

49
00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.931
This guy checked out
all these books before I did.

50
00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.131
Seiji Amasawa, huh?

51
00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:02.870
What kind of person are you?

52
00:04:02.944 --> 00:04:04.879
I wonder if we're anything alike.

53
00:04:16.927 --> 00:04:19.624
[People chattering]

54
00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:23.827
[Mom] Shizuku!

55
00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.267
For heaven sakes, get up!

56
00:04:25.337 --> 00:04:28.397
- I'm leaving.
- [Groaning]

57
00:04:29.641 --> 00:04:31.837
Hey, did you sleep
in your clothes again?

58
00:04:31.911 --> 00:04:33.776
You're so scatterbrained.

59
00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.047
Have a good day.

60
00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.982
Aah! Is it that late?
I'm supposed to meet Yuko.

61
00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:46.121
- [Door opening]
- Ugh! My wallet!

62
00:04:47.329 --> 00:04:50.025
Did you get all the way
down the stairs again, Mom?

63
00:04:50.098 --> 00:04:51.327
Yes!

64
00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.561
Where is it?

65
00:04:53.636 --> 00:04:56.332
Is it by the telephone?

66
00:04:56.405 --> 00:04:58.931
- [Mom] Found it!
- You always leave it there.

67
00:04:59.009 --> 00:05:00.738
[Groaning] I'm gonna be late!

68
00:05:00.811 --> 00:05:03.507
- Don't forget to lock up!
- Who's scatterbrained?

69
00:05:08.152 --> 00:05:09.210
[Gasping]

70
00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.452
Wow! I've never seen a blimp so close.

71
00:05:19.065 --> 00:05:20.930
Today's gonna be great.

72
00:05:38.121 --> 00:05:40.715
[People chattering]

73
00:05:45.529 --> 00:05:47.997
[Sighing] Hot day.

74
00:05:54.672 --> 00:05:57.267
- [Barking]
- Hi, yappy.

75
00:05:57.343 --> 00:05:59.436
Can't you bark any louder than that?

76
00:06:21.136 --> 00:06:24.163
Shizuku! Shizuku! Hey, there.

77
00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.437
Hey, Michiko. Good luck
on your match today.

78
00:06:30.481 --> 00:06:32.642
Hi, Miss Kosaka. Can I come in?

79
00:06:32.716 --> 00:06:36.174
Oh, hi, Shizuku.
What are you doing here?

80
00:06:36.254 --> 00:06:38.154
I need you to do me a favor.

81
00:06:38.223 --> 00:06:40.657
What? It's not something weird, is it?

82
00:06:40.725 --> 00:06:43.661
- Can you open the library, please?
- The library?

83
00:06:43.729 --> 00:06:46.527
Can't you wait until school starts?

84
00:06:46.599 --> 00:06:47.998
No. That's the point.

85
00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:51.128
I decided I was gonna read
20 books over summer vacation,

86
00:06:51.205 --> 00:06:53.833
and the city library
doesn't have the book I want.

87
00:06:53.907 --> 00:06:55.101
It'll just be a second.

88
00:06:55.175 --> 00:06:58.304
Twenty books? What about
your high school entrance exams?

89
00:06:58.379 --> 00:07:00.870
Can't you even pretend
to be studying for them?

90
00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:02.041
Uh, here it is.

91
00:07:02.117 --> 00:07:04.951
Hurry up and bring it here.

92
00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.820
Come on, give me your library card
and the checkout card from the book.

93
00:07:08.891 --> 00:07:10.553
Here you go.

94
00:07:11.728 --> 00:07:13.093
Hey, look at this.

95
00:07:13.163 --> 00:07:15.758
No one's ever checked
this book out before.

96
00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:17.562
No one? What do you know.

97
00:07:17.635 --> 00:07:19.694
I finally beat Seiji Amasawa.

98
00:07:23.842 --> 00:07:24.831
[Gasps]

99
00:07:25.577 --> 00:07:29.708
Donated by... Amasawa?

100
00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:33.843
No way! Do you have any idea
who this Amasawa person is?

101
00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.583
Oh, now look,
you made me make a mistake.

102
00:07:36.657 --> 00:07:39.023
Well, that guy's
probably the book's donor.

103
00:07:39.093 --> 00:07:41.152
I don't know anyone from that long ago.

104
00:07:41.228 --> 00:07:43.720
- Ask one of the older teachers.
- [Girl] Shizuku!

105
00:07:43.798 --> 00:07:46.665
[Groaning] I should have known
you were going to do this.

106
00:07:46.735 --> 00:07:49.364
You said to meet
outside the school, not inside.

107
00:07:49.438 --> 00:07:53.204
I waited in the sun for 15 minutes. Do
you know how many freckles I have now?

108
00:07:53.276 --> 00:07:55.541
- I'm sorry.
- Calm down, Yuko.

109
00:07:55.612 --> 00:07:57.842
You take your freckles
way too seriously.

110
00:07:57.915 --> 00:08:00.383
No, I don't!
It's a major problem for me.

111
00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.113
Aren't either of you
concerned about your exams?

112
00:08:03.188 --> 00:08:05.179
Now get out and go study.

113
00:08:05.957 --> 00:08:07.618
I got it!

114
00:08:08.594 --> 00:08:11.154
Here! [grunting] This way.

115
00:08:11.664 --> 00:08:13.495
[Boy] Kick it harder than that.

116
00:08:13.566 --> 00:08:16.365
I wrote some lyrics
for our graduation ceremony,

117
00:08:16.436 --> 00:08:18.427
but I'm pretty sure that they stink.

118
00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:23.642
♪ Looking over sprawling city

119
00:08:23.711 --> 00:08:25.303
♪ How I do yearn for

120
00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:27.711
♪ Hills and clouds so pretty

121
00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.384
♪ Peaceful bedroom

122
00:08:30.452 --> 00:08:32.511
♪ Window with a view

123
00:08:32.588 --> 00:08:34.989
[both] ♪ Old dog that waits there

124
00:08:35.058 --> 00:08:36.855
♪ Where my dreams come true

125
00:08:36.926 --> 00:08:38.917
♪ Country roads

126
00:08:38.995 --> 00:08:41.327
♪ I think I'll go

127
00:08:41.397 --> 00:08:45.459
♪ Down this path on my own

128
00:08:45.536 --> 00:08:48.004
♪ West Virginia

129
00:08:48.073 --> 00:08:50.064
♪ Mountain mama

130
00:08:50.141 --> 00:08:52.735
♪ Please take me home

131
00:08:52.811 --> 00:08:54.803
♪ Down country roads ♪

132
00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.747
- Hey, it's not bad.
- Yes, it is.

133
00:08:57.817 --> 00:08:59.409
It's boring.

134
00:08:59.485 --> 00:09:01.750
- [Boy] Keep up! Come on!
- I don't think so.

135
00:09:02.489 --> 00:09:04.354
So I wrote another one.

136
00:09:05.425 --> 00:09:07.222
♪ Concrete roads

137
00:09:07.294 --> 00:09:09.627
- ♪ Everywhere I go
- [chuckling]

138
00:09:09.697 --> 00:09:12.222
♪ Covering

139
00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.565
♪ West Tokyo

140
00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:17.367
♪ Chopped down forests

141
00:09:17.439 --> 00:09:19.771
♪ Buried our valleys

142
00:09:19.842 --> 00:09:21.902
[both] ♪ My hometown's

143
00:09:21.978 --> 00:09:25.379
- ♪ Down concrete road ♪
- [laughing]

144
00:09:25.448 --> 00:09:27.974
Let's sing that! [laughing]

145
00:09:28.052 --> 00:09:31.044
Hey, so, why did you want to talk?

146
00:09:31.122 --> 00:09:33.056
Is there something bothering you?

147
00:09:33.124 --> 00:09:36.322
Mmm. Do you think about boys?

148
00:09:36.395 --> 00:09:37.828
No.

149
00:09:37.896 --> 00:09:41.060
We're all studying for exams
and we could help each other.

150
00:09:41.134 --> 00:09:44.592
It would be nice to be with someone
who felt the same way about you.

151
00:09:44.671 --> 00:09:48.005
Yuko, you have a crush on someone.

152
00:09:48.075 --> 00:09:49.406
[Whispering]

153
00:09:49.476 --> 00:09:52.411
- You got a love letter?!
- Ahh! Shh! Not so loud.

154
00:09:52.479 --> 00:09:54.675
So, what's he like? Is he good-looking?

155
00:09:54.749 --> 00:09:56.148
He's from another class.

156
00:09:56.217 --> 00:09:59.277
- Uh, he's sort of good-looking.
- Why not try dating him?

157
00:09:59.354 --> 00:10:01.220
If you don't like him you can stop.

158
00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.621
Yeah, but...

159
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.594
You've got a crush
on someone else, don't you?

160
00:10:06.662 --> 00:10:08.358
[Sighing]

161
00:10:08.432 --> 00:10:12.095
Don't even try to hide it.
You know I'll get it out of you.

162
00:10:12.169 --> 00:10:15.435
It's, uh, Su... Su...

163
00:10:15.506 --> 00:10:18.236
[boy] Shizuku!

164
00:10:18.309 --> 00:10:20.038
Can you throw me my bag?

165
00:10:20.111 --> 00:10:21.636
- [Gasping]
- Sugimura.

166
00:10:21.714 --> 00:10:24.979
[Sugimura] It's that blue one,
on the bench over there.

167
00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:26.540
Come on! Hurry it up!

168
00:10:26.618 --> 00:10:29.281
I got to get back to the game.

169
00:10:29.356 --> 00:10:33.053
Calm down, bench warmer.
You never play anyway.

170
00:10:33.126 --> 00:10:34.992
Hey, I play all the time,

171
00:10:35.062 --> 00:10:38.054
and our team's going to the playoffs,
I'll have you know.

172
00:10:38.132 --> 00:10:39.121
Yuko?

173
00:10:47.744 --> 00:10:49.405
Are you OK?

174
00:10:49.479 --> 00:10:53.416
[Shizuku] So I guess
Sugimura is the guy you like.

175
00:10:53.484 --> 00:10:56.681
[Sighing] How embarrassing.
I ran off like a little girl.

176
00:10:56.754 --> 00:11:00.521
- He must know now.
- No way, Yuko. He's way too dense.

177
00:11:00.592 --> 00:11:03.618
But what about the guy
who wrote you the love letter?

178
00:11:03.695 --> 00:11:06.289
- I think you should go for him.
- [Car passing]

179
00:11:06.364 --> 00:11:10.028
Hmm, I don't know.
I want to think it over.

180
00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:11.433
All right.

181
00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:14.500
[Yuko] You're lucky, Shizuku.

182
00:11:14.574 --> 00:11:17.236
Your parents don't bug you
to study all the time.

183
00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:20.974
- [Shizuku] Sometimes I wish they did.
- [Yuko] Hmm, yeah.

184
00:11:21.048 --> 00:11:22.913
- Oh, no!
- What's the matter?

185
00:11:22.984 --> 00:11:25.043
I lost my book. I must have dropped it.

186
00:11:25.119 --> 00:11:26.747
- You want to ride my bike?
- No!

187
00:11:26.822 --> 00:11:28.915
[Yuko] You'll be late for cram school.

188
00:11:28.991 --> 00:11:31.983
- Call me later, OK?
- [Shizuku] I will!

189
00:11:43.007 --> 00:11:44.304
[Gasping]

190
00:12:04.198 --> 00:12:05.860
[Sighing]

191
00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:12.131
[Gasping] You've got my book.

192
00:12:12.207 --> 00:12:15.177
Oh. This is yours, is it?

193
00:12:19.983 --> 00:12:22.577
Here you go, Shizuku Tsukishima.

194
00:12:22.652 --> 00:12:24.643
What? How do you know my name?

195
00:12:25.388 --> 00:12:27.084
Gee, take a wild guess.

196
00:12:28.259 --> 00:12:30.557
Oh, the checkout card.

197
00:12:30.628 --> 00:12:32.186
By the way, great lyrics.

198
00:12:32.264 --> 00:12:35.062
They're even cornier
than the original version.

199
00:12:39.205 --> 00:12:42.606
[Gasping] You read this?!

200
00:12:43.209 --> 00:12:45.370
Stupid jerk, stupid jerk, stupid jerk.

201
00:12:46.881 --> 00:12:48.974
Stupid jerk, stupid jerk, stupid jerk!

202
00:12:53.154 --> 00:12:54.815
Stupid jerk!

203
00:13:04.834 --> 00:13:07.633
"It's even cornier
than the original version."

204
00:13:08.906 --> 00:13:10.567
Stupid jerk!

205
00:13:27.327 --> 00:13:30.319
[Girls giggling, arguing]

206
00:13:36.404 --> 00:13:37.996
[Sniffling]

207
00:13:48.484 --> 00:13:50.145
Hey, I'm home!

208
00:13:51.287 --> 00:13:53.950
- [Sighing]
- Oh, hey, sis. You're back early.

209
00:13:54.024 --> 00:13:56.356
Ahh, I'm beat.

210
00:13:57.361 --> 00:14:01.628
I grabbed a ride with someone
who's going back to Tokyo.

211
00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.634
- [Bag hits mattress]
- Where's Mom?

212
00:14:03.702 --> 00:14:07.366
She's at an intensive summer course.
Dad's still at work.

213
00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.567
You need to clean up this room, Shizuku,

214
00:14:09.642 --> 00:14:11.907
and you should have
started dinner by now.

215
00:14:11.979 --> 00:14:14.971
- I was just getting to it.
- Ugh! This kitchen is a disaster!

216
00:14:15.048 --> 00:14:17.175
Have you cleaned anything since I left?

217
00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.912
Relax, I'll do it now.

218
00:14:20.555 --> 00:14:21.715
[Water running]

219
00:14:21.789 --> 00:14:25.317
You need to stay on top of this
while Mom's got classes, Shizuku.

220
00:14:29.965 --> 00:14:32.434
After you wash the rice
finish up the laundry.

221
00:14:32.502 --> 00:14:35.062
I'll help you make dinner
after I take a shower.

222
00:14:36.272 --> 00:14:39.800
Auntie said you should come visit her
after you finish your exams.

223
00:14:39.877 --> 00:14:40.866
[Shizuku] Hmm.

224
00:14:40.945 --> 00:14:42.913
- Are you studying?
- Uh-huh.

225
00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.506
You're gonna have
big problems if you slack off

226
00:14:45.584 --> 00:14:48.075
just because Dad and Mom
don't bug you about it.

227
00:14:48.153 --> 00:14:49.916
I'm studying, OK?

228
00:14:49.988 --> 00:14:51.354
[Laughing]

229
00:14:51.424 --> 00:14:54.825
You know, she tried to get me
to bring home some of her soy sauce.

230
00:14:54.894 --> 00:14:57.192
- That's your aunt, all right.
- [Laughing]

231
00:14:57.263 --> 00:14:59.698
[Mom] Didn't the same thing
happen last year?

232
00:14:59.767 --> 00:15:02.759
[Shiho] She made me take home
some miso. Really heavy.

233
00:15:02.836 --> 00:15:05.305
[Dad] Too bad Shizuku
couldn't go with you.

234
00:15:09.978 --> 00:15:11.708
[Grunting]

235
00:15:15.184 --> 00:15:17.710
[Turning off vacuum]

236
00:15:18.922 --> 00:15:21.390
Shizuku, come on, get up.

237
00:15:21.458 --> 00:15:23.255
Vacuum your side of the room.

238
00:15:23.326 --> 00:15:26.057
Then strip the bed,
'cause I'm washing the sheets.

239
00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.121
[Shiho] I'm doing the futons too.

240
00:15:28.199 --> 00:15:32.102
- [Moaning] Hey, where's Mom?
- [Shiho] She left hours ago.

241
00:15:36.341 --> 00:15:40.711
Clear the table when you're done then
take Dad's lunch to him at the library.

242
00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.475
- Hey!
- What do you mean "hey"?

243
00:15:42.549 --> 00:15:44.711
You're going to the library already.

244
00:15:44.785 --> 00:15:47.720
[Shiho] Or do you want me to go instead?

245
00:15:47.788 --> 00:15:51.122
Then you can clean the toilet,
the bathroom and the entryway.

246
00:15:51.193 --> 00:15:53.957
Then you can go to the grocery store,
fold the laundry,

247
00:15:54.029 --> 00:15:57.090
make the beds and cook dinner.
How does that sound?

248
00:16:00.369 --> 00:16:03.031
See you later! Phew!

249
00:16:08.245 --> 00:16:09.907
[Shiho] Shizuku!

250
00:16:10.482 --> 00:16:12.677
Put this in the mailbox for me.

251
00:16:12.751 --> 00:16:14.150
What is it?

252
00:16:14.219 --> 00:16:16.518
Uh, it's mail, stupid.

253
00:16:16.589 --> 00:16:18.853
[Grunting]

254
00:16:21.994 --> 00:16:23.963
[Shiho] You don't need to read it.

255
00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:26.464
Can't you just put it in the mailbox?

256
00:16:26.533 --> 00:16:30.265
- It's a love letter, isn't it?
- Shut up!

257
00:16:30.338 --> 00:16:32.465
[People chattering]

258
00:16:34.342 --> 00:16:36.538
[Boy 1] I don't know
how I'm gonna pass this.

259
00:16:36.612 --> 00:16:38.512
[Boy 2] You gotta read some books.

260
00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:40.707
[Train brakes hissing]

261
00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:45.847
[Conductor whistle blowing]

262
00:17:03.776 --> 00:17:06.244
[Man over PA]
Next stop Suginomiya Station.

263
00:17:06.312 --> 00:17:08.041
Suginomiya Station.

264
00:17:25.668 --> 00:17:27.898
Hey there, cat. You all alone?

265
00:17:32.509 --> 00:17:33.908
So, where are you headed?

266
00:17:37.181 --> 00:17:39.240
See something interesting?

267
00:17:41.085 --> 00:17:43.418
Oh, the silent treatment.

268
00:17:55.903 --> 00:17:58.167
This is my stop. How about you?

269
00:18:02.377 --> 00:18:04.402
So long, snotty.

270
00:18:04.479 --> 00:18:05.468
[Gasping]

271
00:18:06.781 --> 00:18:08.647
[Conductor whistle blowing]

272
00:18:11.387 --> 00:18:12.718
Hey!

273
00:18:38.885 --> 00:18:41.046
He's headed towards the library.

274
00:18:42.623 --> 00:18:44.955
[Engines revving]

275
00:19:02.413 --> 00:19:04.438
[Woman] I'll call you later, all right?

276
00:19:04.515 --> 00:19:08.850
[Sighing] I finally thought I was gonna
get a little adventure around here.

277
00:19:44.461 --> 00:19:45.860
Hey!

278
00:20:09.056 --> 00:20:10.648
[Doorknob rattling]

279
00:20:16.865 --> 00:20:18.264
[Gasping]

280
00:20:21.737 --> 00:20:23.227
Oh!

281
00:20:34.819 --> 00:20:36.286
[Sighing]

282
00:20:39.891 --> 00:20:41.951
What a steep climb.

283
00:20:42.027 --> 00:20:43.858
How far does this thing go?

284
00:20:49.803 --> 00:20:51.395
[Sighing]

285
00:21:02.717 --> 00:21:05.185
Here, kitty.

286
00:21:05.253 --> 00:21:07.245
Here, kitty.

287
00:21:11.461 --> 00:21:14.022
He must live around here somewhere.

288
00:21:29.582 --> 00:21:31.379
[Dog barking]

289
00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.043
Hey!

290
00:21:35.555 --> 00:21:37.216
- [Horn beeping]
- [Gasping]

291
00:21:45.733 --> 00:21:48.100
Where are you going, you crazy cat?

292
00:21:48.170 --> 00:21:49.694
Do you live around here?

293
00:21:52.407 --> 00:21:54.467
[Panting]

294
00:22:08.994 --> 00:22:10.859
What a gorgeous neighborhood.

295
00:22:10.929 --> 00:22:13.524
I never knew there was a place
like this up here.

296
00:22:13.599 --> 00:22:15.931
[Dog barking]

297
00:22:17.069 --> 00:22:20.062
- [Fence rattling]
- [Barking]

298
00:22:27.015 --> 00:22:28.710
[Gasping]

299
00:22:28.783 --> 00:22:31.445
[Barking]

300
00:22:32.288 --> 00:22:33.755
No way.

301
00:22:33.822 --> 00:22:36.222
He came all this way
just to tease that dog?

302
00:22:48.306 --> 00:22:51.764
Hmm. I wonder if that cat
isn't messing with me too.

303
00:22:55.981 --> 00:22:57.642
An antique shop?

304
00:22:57.716 --> 00:22:59.844
He's going shopping now?

305
00:23:43.702 --> 00:23:47.833
Incredible. I had no idea there
were stores like this around here.

306
00:24:16.273 --> 00:24:19.038
What a fantastic statue.

307
00:24:25.584 --> 00:24:28.553
You're not the cat
I was following, are you?

308
00:24:30.289 --> 00:24:31.951
[Gasping]

309
00:24:37.364 --> 00:24:38.696
[Thump]

310
00:24:40.768 --> 00:24:42.963
- Oh, hello there.
- I'm sorry.

311
00:24:43.037 --> 00:24:45.233
No, please, it's good to have visitors.

312
00:24:45.307 --> 00:24:47.036
Look around as much as you like.

313
00:24:47.109 --> 00:24:48.974
The Baron is bored too.

314
00:24:50.479 --> 00:24:53.574
The Baron? Is that the name
of the statue over here?

315
00:24:53.650 --> 00:24:55.845
Yeah. Baron Humbert von Joekkingen.

316
00:24:55.919 --> 00:24:57.911
Good name, don't you think?

317
00:25:01.659 --> 00:25:03.718
[Creaking]

318
00:25:06.331 --> 00:25:09.459
- [Creaking]
- [Man] Oh, thanks.

319
00:25:09.534 --> 00:25:12.003
Don't worry, though.
I do this all the time.

320
00:25:12.071 --> 00:25:13.402
Great clock.

321
00:25:13.473 --> 00:25:17.808
It was found in an abandoned castle
all covered with rust.

322
00:25:17.878 --> 00:25:19.072
Look at this.

323
00:25:21.815 --> 00:25:23.807
[Gasping] Beautiful.

324
00:25:23.885 --> 00:25:25.819
So, what does it do?

325
00:25:25.887 --> 00:25:28.481
[Chuckling]

326
00:25:28.556 --> 00:25:30.752
It might not do anything.

327
00:25:30.826 --> 00:25:33.488
- I just finished restoring this.
- [Cranking]

328
00:25:33.562 --> 00:25:35.757
I haven't tried it out yet.

329
00:25:35.831 --> 00:25:38.300
[Clock ticking]

330
00:25:45.176 --> 00:25:49.442
- [Calliope music playing]
- [Ticking]

331
00:25:49.514 --> 00:25:51.039
[Gasping]

332
00:25:52.818 --> 00:25:56.549
[Cranking]

333
00:26:02.829 --> 00:26:05.765
[Tapping]

334
00:26:10.839 --> 00:26:13.330
Dwarves in a jewel mine,
just like a fairy tale.

335
00:26:13.408 --> 00:26:14.807
You like fairy tales.

336
00:26:14.876 --> 00:26:18.938
This clock has a terribly romantic
fairy tale that goes with it.

337
00:26:20.416 --> 00:26:22.611
Watch what happens on the clock face...

338
00:26:22.685 --> 00:26:25.086
At least I hope something happens.

339
00:26:29.894 --> 00:26:32.488
[Whirring]

340
00:26:34.566 --> 00:26:38.230
[Chiming]

341
00:26:42.308 --> 00:26:43.571
What is that?

342
00:26:43.643 --> 00:26:46.771
Stand up here on the ladder,
then you can see better.

343
00:26:46.847 --> 00:26:48.178
OK.

344
00:26:49.316 --> 00:26:50.978
[Gasping]

345
00:26:51.486 --> 00:26:53.579
Oh, it's a fairy.

346
00:26:53.654 --> 00:26:57.716
[Man] She is now, but soon
she'll turn back into a sheep.

347
00:27:04.200 --> 00:27:06.293
The two of them are in love,
aren't they?

348
00:27:06.369 --> 00:27:08.929
Mm-hmm. But they are always apart.

349
00:27:09.005 --> 00:27:11.440
He's king of the dwarves
and lives underground

350
00:27:11.509 --> 00:27:14.342
while she's cursed to live as a sheep.

351
00:27:14.411 --> 00:27:17.142
Only while the clock strikes 12:00
is she a fairy.

352
00:27:17.215 --> 00:27:19.479
So the king appears at that moment

353
00:27:19.551 --> 00:27:22.749
just to catch a glimpse
of the girl he fell in love with.

354
00:27:22.822 --> 00:27:26.223
What do you bet that the artisan
who made this clock

355
00:27:26.292 --> 00:27:29.751
was separated from the love of his life?

356
00:27:29.830 --> 00:27:33.891
[Shizuku] That must be why
their sadness feels so real.

357
00:27:33.967 --> 00:27:36.562
- [Ticking]
- [Gasping]

358
00:27:36.638 --> 00:27:38.970
That clock isn't on time, is it?

359
00:27:39.040 --> 00:27:41.304
No. It's about five minutes too slow.

360
00:27:41.376 --> 00:27:43.572
- Oh, no!
- Whoa!

361
00:27:43.646 --> 00:27:46.638
I've got to get to the library!

362
00:27:46.715 --> 00:27:49.082
I'm sorry, do you mind
if I come again later?

363
00:27:49.152 --> 00:27:52.553
Sure. But it's better to go left
to get to the library.

364
00:27:52.622 --> 00:27:53.953
[Shizuku squealing]

365
00:28:05.203 --> 00:28:08.138
Oh, good! I'm right above the library.

366
00:28:08.206 --> 00:28:10.198
[Panting]

367
00:28:12.412 --> 00:28:13.936
What a great place that was.

368
00:28:14.013 --> 00:28:16.346
It was like straight
out of a fairy tale.

369
00:28:17.885 --> 00:28:20.217
- That was amazing!
- [Beeping]

370
00:28:21.756 --> 00:28:23.690
[Boy] Shizuku Tsukishima!

371
00:28:25.327 --> 00:28:26.658
[Brakes squealing]

372
00:28:26.728 --> 00:28:28.253
Hey, this is yours, isn't it?

373
00:28:28.331 --> 00:28:30.697
Huh? Aah!

374
00:28:30.766 --> 00:28:32.290
Uh...

375
00:28:33.502 --> 00:28:35.630
You're kind of forgetful, aren't you?

376
00:28:35.706 --> 00:28:37.901
Uh, thanks, but how did you get this?

377
00:28:37.975 --> 00:28:39.806
Take a wild guess.

378
00:28:41.411 --> 00:28:43.505
That man, do you know him?

379
00:28:43.581 --> 00:28:44.912
Is he your grandpa?

380
00:28:44.983 --> 00:28:47.543
You must eat like a pig.
That lunch is enormous.

381
00:28:47.619 --> 00:28:48.985
Huh?

382
00:28:49.054 --> 00:28:50.851
[Gasping] Hey you!

383
00:28:50.923 --> 00:28:54.552
♪ Concrete roads
Everywhere I go ♪

384
00:28:55.729 --> 00:28:58.095
It's my dad's, you jerk!

385
00:29:00.066 --> 00:29:02.399
Hey, thanks. You brought my lunch.

386
00:29:04.705 --> 00:29:07.606
What's wrong? Why the sour face?

387
00:29:07.675 --> 00:29:10.645
- It's hard to explain.
- And?

388
00:29:10.712 --> 00:29:14.444
I was having an extraordinary day,
like I was living in a fairy tale,

389
00:29:14.517 --> 00:29:18.044
then some jerk talked to me
for two seconds and ruined everything.

390
00:29:18.121 --> 00:29:20.316
[Chuckling] Sounds complicated.

391
00:29:21.625 --> 00:29:23.923
Are you going to check out
some books today?

392
00:29:23.994 --> 00:29:25.859
Yeah. I just have seven more to go.

393
00:29:25.929 --> 00:29:29.263
You never stop reading. You want
to take some time out for lunch?

394
00:29:29.334 --> 00:29:32.132
- I'll eat later.
- OK, then. See you later.

395
00:29:33.571 --> 00:29:34.903
[Man coughing]

396
00:29:53.996 --> 00:29:56.191
[Shizuku] Seiji Amasawa.

397
00:29:56.265 --> 00:30:00.794
Wow. Is there any book here
this guy hasn't checked out?

398
00:30:00.870 --> 00:30:03.532
I wonder what kind of person he is.

399
00:30:06.476 --> 00:30:09.241
- No way! Not that jerk!
- [Murmuring]

400
00:30:11.449 --> 00:30:14.078
- [Murmuring]
- [Woman] Shh!

401
00:30:32.439 --> 00:30:34.635
[Leaves rustling]

402
00:30:34.709 --> 00:30:36.768
- Aah!
- [Wind gusting]

403
00:30:54.932 --> 00:30:57.730
[Thunder rumbling]

404
00:31:02.241 --> 00:31:04.766
[Mom] Shizuku, hurry up!

405
00:31:06.078 --> 00:31:08.274
Oh! We're going to be late!

406
00:31:08.348 --> 00:31:09.906
Hurry, get the umbrellas.

407
00:31:13.087 --> 00:31:15.749
The first day of the semester
and it has to rain.

408
00:31:15.823 --> 00:31:18.383
- [Girls laughing]
- [Shizuku] Stop complaining.

409
00:31:18.459 --> 00:31:20.655
You're going to school
because you want to.

410
00:31:20.729 --> 00:31:22.492
- Yes, ma'am.
- Study hard.

411
00:31:22.564 --> 00:31:24.361
You can count on me.

412
00:31:32.708 --> 00:31:34.574
- Shizuku!
- Hey, Yuko!

413
00:31:34.645 --> 00:31:37.205
Hurry up! I don't want to be late
for our first day.

414
00:31:37.281 --> 00:31:40.046
I can't believe how many tests
we have to take.

415
00:31:40.118 --> 00:31:42.450
It's one thing or another every day.

416
00:31:47.059 --> 00:31:49.721
- So, did you answer the letter?
- Mm-mmm.

417
00:31:49.795 --> 00:31:51.490
Have you made up your mind yet?

418
00:31:51.564 --> 00:31:53.999
Yeah. I decided I don't want
to go out with him.

419
00:31:54.067 --> 00:31:57.730
OK. Yeah, maybe that's best.

420
00:31:57.804 --> 00:32:00.399
- Sugimura!
- [Gasping]

421
00:32:00.474 --> 00:32:02.203
You're gonna be late!

422
00:32:02.276 --> 00:32:04.471
Calm down, we know!

423
00:32:13.423 --> 00:32:16.950
- OK, everybody, pencils down.
- [Students groaning]

424
00:32:17.026 --> 00:32:19.495
[Bell chiming]

425
00:32:22.633 --> 00:32:25.397
- Regular classes this afternoon.
- Hey, Jun, Daizo.

426
00:32:25.469 --> 00:32:27.563
Let's eat fast so we can get outside.

427
00:32:27.639 --> 00:32:30.301
Let's eat lunch
in Miss Kosaka's office, OK?

428
00:32:30.375 --> 00:32:32.606
Can we stop
by the teachers' lounge first?

429
00:32:32.678 --> 00:32:34.908
- I guess so.
- Hey, Shizuku, check it out!

430
00:32:34.981 --> 00:32:37.711
- What?
- I totally aced that test.

431
00:32:37.783 --> 00:32:39.081
Well, good for you.

432
00:32:39.152 --> 00:32:42.485
Everything I studied was on the test
and I barely studied.

433
00:32:42.556 --> 00:32:44.922
So you're not just
a bench warmer after all.

434
00:32:44.992 --> 00:32:47.257
Yuko's good at guessing what's on tests.

435
00:32:47.328 --> 00:32:50.456
- You should study with her sometime.
- Study with her?

436
00:32:50.531 --> 00:32:52.591
- Sugimura, Sugimura!
- What's up?

437
00:32:52.668 --> 00:32:55.637
- [Boy] Did you see this?
- Let's go, Shizuku.

438
00:33:00.677 --> 00:33:02.804
I can't believe you said that, Shizuku.

439
00:33:02.879 --> 00:33:04.005
What's the problem?

440
00:33:04.080 --> 00:33:06.709
I've never been good
at guessing what's on tests.

441
00:33:06.784 --> 00:33:07.842
[Chuckling] Sorry.

442
00:33:08.753 --> 00:33:10.152
Excuse us.

443
00:33:12.891 --> 00:33:14.882
You want to know who donated a book?

444
00:33:14.960 --> 00:33:17.520
I don't think I'd remember
something like that.

445
00:33:17.596 --> 00:33:19.963
I hate to interrupt you
while you're eating.

446
00:33:20.033 --> 00:33:22.524
- Look at this stamp here.
- Hmm? Well...

447
00:33:22.602 --> 00:33:23.933
Let's see.

448
00:33:26.373 --> 00:33:30.833
Oh, Dr. Amasawa, sure. I've read
this book too. It's quite a good one.

449
00:33:30.911 --> 00:33:32.504
Yes, it's great.

450
00:33:32.580 --> 00:33:35.845
So, is there anything that you can
tell me about Dr. Amasawa?

451
00:33:35.917 --> 00:33:37.384
Let me see if I can remember.

452
00:33:37.452 --> 00:33:39.648
I think he was chairman of the PTA.

453
00:33:39.722 --> 00:33:40.984
The PTA, huh?

454
00:33:41.057 --> 00:33:44.049
Would you happen to remember
Dr. Amasawa's first name?

455
00:33:44.126 --> 00:33:45.719
First name? Let's see.

456
00:33:45.796 --> 00:33:49.664
Mr. Kimura, do you happen to
remember Dr. Amasawa's first name?

457
00:33:49.733 --> 00:33:53.363
Dr. Amasawa. I'm pretty sure
it's Koichi. Koichi Amasawa.

458
00:33:53.438 --> 00:33:55.372
Koichi Amasawa.

459
00:33:55.440 --> 00:33:58.604
Shizuku, Dr. Amasawa's son
goes to school here.

460
00:33:58.677 --> 00:34:01.805
There's a chance you could
have met him. He's in your grade.

461
00:34:01.880 --> 00:34:03.347
Huh? Uh... I...

462
00:34:03.415 --> 00:34:05.543
I gotta go. Thank you very much!

463
00:34:06.553 --> 00:34:08.043
Uh, excuse us.

464
00:34:08.755 --> 00:34:10.416
Oh! Excuse me.

465
00:34:10.490 --> 00:34:12.049
[Sighing]

466
00:34:12.126 --> 00:34:15.323
[Yuko] Shizuku! What's wrong with you?

467
00:34:15.396 --> 00:34:18.389
[Panting] It can't be him.

468
00:34:18.467 --> 00:34:20.833
What in the world are you talking about?

469
00:34:20.902 --> 00:34:23.962
You are acting like a total weirdo.

470
00:34:24.039 --> 00:34:26.508
I'm sorry. [sighing]

471
00:34:35.119 --> 00:34:37.383
Shizuku, now what are you doing?

472
00:34:54.074 --> 00:34:57.009
What a complete jerk!
Do you know what that guy's name is?

473
00:34:57.077 --> 00:34:59.512
No. He's not in our class.
What's the big deal?

474
00:34:59.580 --> 00:35:02.242
That jerk better not
be Dr. Amasawa's son.

475
00:35:02.316 --> 00:35:03.578
[Laughing]

476
00:35:03.651 --> 00:35:06.553
[Girl] Shizuku chasing down boys?
I don't believe it.

477
00:35:06.622 --> 00:35:09.386
[Yuko] I had to run after her
carrying her lunchbox.

478
00:35:10.059 --> 00:35:12.494
So Shizuku has a crush on someone, eh?

479
00:35:12.562 --> 00:35:15.395
Miss Kosaka, can you believe
she's finally interested

480
00:35:15.465 --> 00:35:17.297
in something other than a book?

481
00:35:17.368 --> 00:35:20.929
- I'm not interested. He's a jerk!
- What if he checked out those books?

482
00:35:21.005 --> 00:35:23.975
- He's your perfect match.
- Like a fairy tale.

483
00:35:24.042 --> 00:35:25.839
If it's him, it's a horror story.

484
00:35:25.911 --> 00:35:30.075
So, tell us, what's the name of this guy
who checked out all the books, Yuko?

485
00:35:31.184 --> 00:35:33.584
- Yuko.
- I can't remember exactly.

486
00:35:33.653 --> 00:35:36.919
There was a "ma" in it,
or maybe it was a "wa."

487
00:35:36.990 --> 00:35:39.652
Ama... Just say it, Shizuku!

488
00:35:39.726 --> 00:35:42.718
- No way.
- Shizuku is such a great storyteller,

489
00:35:42.796 --> 00:35:45.527
but now that the story is about her,
she won't say a word.

490
00:35:45.600 --> 00:35:48.626
You can't hide the fact
you're in love, Shizuku.

491
00:35:49.270 --> 00:35:52.672
The look on your face shows
your heart suffers with every beat.

492
00:35:52.741 --> 00:35:55.835
[Mouth full] How romantic.
You are in love.

493
00:35:56.613 --> 00:35:59.138
Go ahead, make fun of me if you want to.

494
00:35:59.216 --> 00:36:02.344
Too bad. I was gonna show you
my lyrics for Country Roads.

495
00:36:02.419 --> 00:36:04.820
- You're finished?
- Let me see! Let me see!

496
00:36:06.090 --> 00:36:10.323
Great Shizuku, master of writing,
we shall make fun of you no more.

497
00:36:10.395 --> 00:36:13.296
- Please grace us with your words.
- That's better.

498
00:36:14.099 --> 00:36:16.158
I don't know if it's any good, though.

499
00:36:17.103 --> 00:36:19.901
And it might not be
appropriate for graduation.

500
00:36:19.973 --> 00:36:22.567
I just tried to write something
from the heart.

501
00:36:22.642 --> 00:36:24.975
This is so good, Shizuku.

502
00:36:25.045 --> 00:36:27.445
♪ Country roads

503
00:36:27.515 --> 00:36:30.178
[girls] ♪ I think I'll go

504
00:36:30.252 --> 00:36:35.349
♪ Down this path on my own

505
00:36:35.423 --> 00:36:37.858
♪ My inspiration

506
00:36:37.927 --> 00:36:40.657
♪ The road less taken

507
00:36:40.730 --> 00:36:43.063
♪ But this is my

508
00:36:43.133 --> 00:36:45.363
♪ Country road ♪

509
00:36:45.435 --> 00:36:48.097
It's great, Shizuku. I love it!

510
00:36:48.172 --> 00:36:50.107
The lyrics aren't too corny?

511
00:36:50.175 --> 00:36:51.665
No. They're wonderful.

512
00:36:51.743 --> 00:36:53.802
You really have a gift for writing.

513
00:36:53.878 --> 00:36:56.643
Reading all those books
actually did her some good.

514
00:36:56.715 --> 00:36:59.275
- You sure they're OK?
- They're from the heart.

515
00:36:59.351 --> 00:37:01.342
Yeah. I really like this part:

516
00:37:01.420 --> 00:37:03.685
"I dreamed of living alone but fearless.

517
00:37:03.757 --> 00:37:06.555
- [Bell chiming]
- Secret longing to be courageous.

518
00:37:06.626 --> 00:37:08.719
Loneliness kept bottled up inside..."

519
00:37:08.795 --> 00:37:11.424
- Ladies, that's the bell.
- [Girls] Yes, ma'am.

520
00:37:17.973 --> 00:37:20.373
Ahh! I love being a writer!

521
00:37:20.442 --> 00:37:21.875
[Yuko] Shizuku!

522
00:37:21.944 --> 00:37:24.209
Do you want to come with us
to the glee club?

523
00:37:24.280 --> 00:37:26.840
- We're gonna show them your lyrics.
- No, thanks.

524
00:37:26.916 --> 00:37:29.442
I want to check out some books
from the library.

525
00:37:29.520 --> 00:37:31.511
We've got a test tomorrow, you know.

526
00:37:31.589 --> 00:37:34.387
- I'll study when I get home.
- [Yuko] Yeah, right.

527
00:37:34.458 --> 00:37:36.620
- See you later.
- See ya!

528
00:38:05.327 --> 00:38:07.659
[Girls chattering in hallway]

529
00:38:12.102 --> 00:38:13.501
Hey, Yuko.

530
00:38:15.106 --> 00:38:19.008
Uh, sorry to bother you
but, uh, can we talk?

531
00:38:20.845 --> 00:38:22.370
Mm-hmm.

532
00:38:29.522 --> 00:38:31.922
I was afraid it would be closed.

533
00:38:31.991 --> 00:38:34.323
I hope that old man's doing all right.

534
00:38:45.974 --> 00:38:48.967
[Groaning] The Baron's gone.

535
00:38:49.045 --> 00:38:50.706
Someone must have bought him.

536
00:38:56.787 --> 00:39:00.052
"Mr. Nishi's Antique Shop."

537
00:39:00.123 --> 00:39:01.489
Oh, thank goodness.

538
00:39:01.559 --> 00:39:04.221
That jerk's name isn't Amasawa.
It's Nishi.

539
00:39:04.295 --> 00:39:06.627
- [Bicycle brakes squealing]
- [Gasping]

540
00:39:11.036 --> 00:39:12.435
[Sighing]

541
00:39:16.776 --> 00:39:19.711
- [Music playing]
- [Shiho] Shizuku!

542
00:39:19.779 --> 00:39:22.305
Shizuku, Yuko's on the phone.

543
00:39:24.452 --> 00:39:25.441
Hey!

544
00:39:26.120 --> 00:39:27.952
Phone call. Can't you hear anything?

545
00:39:28.657 --> 00:39:31.455
I keep telling you
you're gonna ruin your hearing.

546
00:39:31.526 --> 00:39:33.790
Hello? What?

547
00:39:33.862 --> 00:39:36.058
I can't really hear you.

548
00:39:36.132 --> 00:39:39.329
Mm-hmm. Don't worry about it, Yuko.

549
00:39:39.402 --> 00:39:41.428
Mm-hmm. I'll be right there.

550
00:39:41.505 --> 00:39:44.167
- Where are you going?
- Just down the street.

551
00:39:44.241 --> 00:39:46.607
[Door rattling]

552
00:39:50.482 --> 00:39:54.476
- Yuko, what happened?
- [Sobbing] Shizuku.

553
00:39:54.553 --> 00:39:57.613
What is it? Why... Why are you crying?

554
00:39:57.690 --> 00:40:00.090
I talked to Sugimura,

555
00:40:00.159 --> 00:40:03.061
and he's friends with the guy
who wrote me that letter,

556
00:40:03.130 --> 00:40:07.123
so he tried to convince me to go out
with his friend. [crying]

557
00:40:07.201 --> 00:40:10.136
What? [groaning]

558
00:40:10.204 --> 00:40:14.107
Go out with your friend?
How could you say that to me?!

559
00:40:14.176 --> 00:40:16.701
- [Crying]
- What?

560
00:40:19.715 --> 00:40:22.310
That jerk.
I can't believe he's that stupid.

561
00:40:22.385 --> 00:40:24.512
But I don't think he did it to hurt you.

562
00:40:24.587 --> 00:40:27.716
He's just a dope.
He has no idea that you like him.

563
00:40:28.726 --> 00:40:31.194
[Sighing] I better
apologize to him, I guess.

564
00:40:31.262 --> 00:40:34.790
But there's no way I can go to school
with my face looking like this.

565
00:40:34.866 --> 00:40:36.959
I'm going to have to stay home tomorrow.

566
00:40:37.035 --> 00:40:39.128
- We've got tests, you know.
- Mm-hmm.

567
00:40:40.273 --> 00:40:41.740
OK.

568
00:41:00.362 --> 00:41:01.693
[Whispering] Idiot.

569
00:41:03.966 --> 00:41:05.627
What did I do?

570
00:41:07.370 --> 00:41:08.894
That was pretty easy, huh?

571
00:41:08.972 --> 00:41:12.373
- Headed to the library again?
- No. I'm gonna go check on Yuko.

572
00:41:12.442 --> 00:41:14.377
Oh, tell her I hope she feels better.

573
00:41:14.445 --> 00:41:15.844
- I will. See ya.
- Bye-bye.

574
00:41:23.255 --> 00:41:25.655
[Sugimura] Shizuku!

575
00:41:25.724 --> 00:41:27.454
Wait up!

576
00:41:28.528 --> 00:41:30.189
Whoa!

577
00:41:33.801 --> 00:41:36.201
I need to talk to you about Yuko.

578
00:41:42.677 --> 00:41:46.079
And then all of a sudden
she starts crying her head off.

579
00:41:46.148 --> 00:41:48.616
So, what did I say
that was so terrible, huh?

580
00:41:49.886 --> 00:41:51.353
Just think about it.

581
00:41:51.420 --> 00:41:53.855
Remember when Yuko said,
"Date your friend?

582
00:41:53.924 --> 00:41:56.051
- How could you say that to me?"
- Mm-hmm.

583
00:41:56.126 --> 00:41:59.221
All I said was he's a good guy.
She should give him a chance.

584
00:41:59.297 --> 00:42:00.559
Get a clue!

585
00:42:00.632 --> 00:42:04.033
What Yuko was saying was that she
didn't want to hear that from you.

586
00:42:04.102 --> 00:42:07.561
- You know what that means, don't you?
- I don't speak girl code!

587
00:42:07.640 --> 00:42:09.437
Why don't you spell it out for me?

588
00:42:09.508 --> 00:42:11.908
[Grunting] I can't believe
you're this dense!

589
00:42:11.977 --> 00:42:14.037
What it means is Yuko
has a crush on you.

590
00:42:14.114 --> 00:42:18.050
What? Are you sure?
I didn't pick up on that.

591
00:42:18.118 --> 00:42:21.316
Are you blind? She stayed home
from school, you know.

592
00:42:21.389 --> 00:42:23.550
She even missed a test
on account of you.

593
00:42:23.624 --> 00:42:27.561
But, it's that...
You're the one I'm in love with!

594
00:42:27.629 --> 00:42:29.563
[Gasping] What?

595
00:42:29.631 --> 00:42:31.929
Come on, quit joking around, will you?

596
00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:35.801
I'm not joking. I've been in love with
you for years. Haven't you noticed?

597
00:42:35.872 --> 00:42:39.809
But you can't fall for me.
That just doesn't happen.

598
00:42:39.877 --> 00:42:43.142
Don't you like me at all?
Or is there someone else you love?

599
00:42:43.213 --> 00:42:46.342
I'm not in love with anybody,

600
00:42:46.418 --> 00:42:49.444
but Yuko, she'll... I gotta go!

601
00:42:49.521 --> 00:42:51.614
Wait a minute! Forget Yuko!

602
00:42:51.690 --> 00:42:52.817
Do you like me?

603
00:42:52.892 --> 00:42:55.486
Of course I like you.
We've been friends for years.

604
00:42:55.561 --> 00:42:59.726
But Yuko and I are best friends,
so that's the way it's gonna stay, OK?

605
00:43:01.568 --> 00:43:04.731
You understand? Or do I have
to spell it out some more?

606
00:43:10.511 --> 00:43:12.707
No. I understand.

607
00:43:12.781 --> 00:43:15.648
We'll just be friends.

608
00:43:22.392 --> 00:43:25.726
[Sugimura] I'm sorry.
I'll never mention it again.

609
00:43:26.864 --> 00:43:29.332
[Bird singing]

610
00:43:43.549 --> 00:43:46.348
[Barking]

611
00:44:03.139 --> 00:44:04.539
[Bag hits floor]

612
00:44:06.710 --> 00:44:08.041
[Sighing]

613
00:44:10.847 --> 00:44:13.442
[Crying] You idiot!

614
00:44:13.518 --> 00:44:16.112
You're the one who's dense.

615
00:44:22.428 --> 00:44:24.522
[Door opening]

616
00:44:24.597 --> 00:44:27.589
[Woman] Oh, Mrs. Tsukishima,
I've got a package for you.

617
00:44:27.667 --> 00:44:29.134
The mailman left it with me.

618
00:44:29.202 --> 00:44:31.603
[Mom] Oh, thanks. Sorry to trouble you.

619
00:44:33.741 --> 00:44:34.730
[Door closing]

620
00:44:44.387 --> 00:44:46.218
[Woman] Thanks so much for these.

621
00:44:46.289 --> 00:44:48.985
No problem. There's way
too much for us to eat.

622
00:44:50.293 --> 00:44:51.818
Oh, you're home.

623
00:44:51.895 --> 00:44:53.453
Shizuku.

624
00:46:14.523 --> 00:46:16.515
Hi, cat.

625
00:46:18.195 --> 00:46:20.527
Did you get locked out of your house?

626
00:46:23.067 --> 00:46:25.729
So, what happened?
Did everyone forget about you?

627
00:46:25.803 --> 00:46:27.668
Would you like some company?

628
00:46:30.209 --> 00:46:32.734
You're not very nice, are you, cat?

629
00:46:32.811 --> 00:46:34.039
Neither am I.

630
00:46:36.149 --> 00:46:38.879
I used to be nice and friendly
and a grade-A student.

631
00:46:38.952 --> 00:46:42.479
Now I just goof around reading books
and writing stupid lyrics.

632
00:46:42.555 --> 00:46:43.921
I don't know what's wrong.

633
00:46:43.991 --> 00:46:46.892
Even reading books isn't
as much fun as it used to be.

634
00:46:46.961 --> 00:46:49.259
Now when I read a little voice
inside me says,

635
00:46:49.331 --> 00:46:52.129
"Things never turn out
like they do in fairy tales."

636
00:46:52.200 --> 00:46:53.599
I miss the old me.

637
00:46:55.972 --> 00:46:58.167
[Panting]

638
00:47:15.660 --> 00:47:17.720
[Footsteps]

639
00:47:18.864 --> 00:47:20.798
Shizuku Tsukishima.

640
00:47:20.866 --> 00:47:22.197
Hi.

641
00:47:22.268 --> 00:47:24.737
I'm surprised Moon lets you pet him.

642
00:47:24.804 --> 00:47:27.068
You don't like anyone, do you, Moon?

643
00:47:27.140 --> 00:47:28.607
So Moon is his name?

644
00:47:28.675 --> 00:47:32.612
He looks like a full moon, doesn't he?
Especially from that angle.

645
00:47:32.680 --> 00:47:35.205
But I've heard him called
a few other names too.

646
00:47:35.283 --> 00:47:37.878
[Barking]

647
00:47:37.953 --> 00:47:40.217
What do you mean?
Doesn't he belong to you?

648
00:47:40.289 --> 00:47:42.224
Nope. He doesn't belong to anybody.

649
00:47:42.292 --> 00:47:46.058
He just wanders around our neighborhood
and lives in different houses.

650
00:47:46.129 --> 00:47:48.222
I've heard our neighbors call him Muta.

651
00:47:48.298 --> 00:47:51.325
Hmm. So he's a vagabond.

652
00:47:51.402 --> 00:47:55.499
That's right! I saw him riding around
on the train the other day.

653
00:47:55.573 --> 00:47:57.564
- The train?
- Yeah.

654
00:47:57.642 --> 00:47:59.371
He was taking a trip all by himself,

655
00:47:59.444 --> 00:48:01.605
he got off at my stop
and I followed him here.

656
00:48:01.680 --> 00:48:04.479
I was so excited
when he led me to this store.

657
00:48:04.550 --> 00:48:07.519
It was like something
straight out of a fairy tale.

658
00:48:09.256 --> 00:48:12.384
I guess I shouldn't have said
those bad things about him.

659
00:48:12.459 --> 00:48:14.120
I said he was mean like me.

660
00:48:14.194 --> 00:48:18.256
What? Moon's not like you.
He's not like you at all.

661
00:48:18.333 --> 00:48:21.667
I... I mean, the cat's
really kind of crazy.

662
00:48:23.005 --> 00:48:25.064
[Sighing]

663
00:48:28.945 --> 00:48:30.606
- So, I...
- Is your?

664
00:48:32.682 --> 00:48:34.081
Is your grandfather OK?

665
00:48:34.150 --> 00:48:37.143
His shop has been closed
for so long. I hope he's not sick.

666
00:48:37.221 --> 00:48:39.951
Yeah, he's fine.
He just likes to keep weird hours.

667
00:48:40.024 --> 00:48:42.550
His store is closed
more often than it's open.

668
00:48:42.627 --> 00:48:46.427
I peeked in the window and saw the Baron
is not sitting on the table anymore.

669
00:48:46.498 --> 00:48:49.366
- Did somebody buy him?
- You mean that cat statue?

670
00:48:49.435 --> 00:48:50.800
Wanna see him? Come on.

671
00:48:58.645 --> 00:49:00.636
[Door creaking]

672
00:49:01.449 --> 00:49:03.110
Can you close the door?

673
00:49:11.060 --> 00:49:12.721
[Gasping]

674
00:49:18.935 --> 00:49:20.402
This way.

675
00:49:22.673 --> 00:49:25.471
Wow. It's almost like we're in the sky.

676
00:49:31.817 --> 00:49:34.810
You're not afraid of heights,
are you, Shizuku?

677
00:49:35.422 --> 00:49:37.913
No. I love it up here. It's inspiring.

678
00:49:44.365 --> 00:49:48.166
From the balcony this time of day
is the prettiest. Come on.

679
00:50:11.596 --> 00:50:12.927
Here we are.

680
00:50:12.997 --> 00:50:16.263
- You can sit if you like.
- Hey, the clock is gone.

681
00:50:16.335 --> 00:50:20.739
Oh, the big grandfather clock.
We delivered it today.

682
00:50:20.807 --> 00:50:22.331
Here, have a look.

683
00:50:22.409 --> 00:50:23.876
So who bought the clock?

684
00:50:23.944 --> 00:50:26.538
No one. It was just here
for a repair job.

685
00:50:26.613 --> 00:50:29.344
I see. Too bad. It was beautiful.

686
00:50:29.417 --> 00:50:31.544
It took Grandpa three years to fix it.

687
00:50:31.619 --> 00:50:34.111
He finished it the day
you left your lunch here.

688
00:50:34.189 --> 00:50:35.554
Hey, about that lunch...

689
00:50:35.624 --> 00:50:38.286
I know it wasn't yours
and you don't eat like a pig.

690
00:50:38.360 --> 00:50:41.228
Come over here and have a look
into the Baron's eyes.

691
00:50:43.032 --> 00:50:45.023
Hurry up. The sun's starting to set.

692
00:50:50.574 --> 00:50:51.905
Wow.

693
00:50:57.182 --> 00:51:00.118
Pretty cool, huh?
It's actually an accident.

694
00:51:00.186 --> 00:51:03.246
Sometimes the eyes get flawed
when they're installed,

695
00:51:03.322 --> 00:51:06.451
- then they refract the light like that.
- That's amazing.

696
00:51:06.527 --> 00:51:09.928
Grandpa will never sell the Baron.
He wants to find its partner.

697
00:51:09.997 --> 00:51:11.862
There's another one?

698
00:51:11.932 --> 00:51:16.199
Yeah. He says that her name
is Louise, but that's about it.

699
00:51:16.271 --> 00:51:19.764
Look as long as you like.
I'm going downstairs.

700
00:51:23.145 --> 00:51:25.613
The light switch is over there
if you need it.

701
00:51:38.563 --> 00:51:41.499
So, Baron, let's hear about this Louise.

702
00:51:41.567 --> 00:51:43.967
Is she an old girlfriend
of yours or something?

703
00:51:44.036 --> 00:51:46.562
You look like you're
all dressed up for a wedding.

704
00:51:46.639 --> 00:51:49.938
Did she leave you at the altar?
Did someone kidnap her?

705
00:51:50.009 --> 00:51:53.969
There's a sad story there.
I'll have to figure it out for myself.

706
00:52:23.982 --> 00:52:26.451
[Scraping]

707
00:52:56.185 --> 00:52:58.050
Hey. Had enough?

708
00:52:58.121 --> 00:52:59.851
Mm-hmm. Thank you.

709
00:52:59.923 --> 00:53:03.120
So, is that a real violin you're making?

710
00:53:03.193 --> 00:53:05.253
Oh. Yeah.

711
00:53:06.665 --> 00:53:08.826
- Can I see?
- Sure.

712
00:53:12.338 --> 00:53:13.999
It's nearly finished.

713
00:53:14.073 --> 00:53:15.267
Wow!

714
00:53:15.341 --> 00:53:18.242
You carved the entire thing
yourself, by hand?

715
00:53:18.312 --> 00:53:21.475
- How else would you do it?
- That is amazing.

716
00:53:21.548 --> 00:53:25.007
They've been making violins
the exact same way for 300 years,

717
00:53:25.086 --> 00:53:27.054
but whether or not
they sound any good

718
00:53:27.121 --> 00:53:29.749
is totally dependent
on the craftsman's skill.

719
00:53:29.824 --> 00:53:31.884
Did you make all those violins?

720
00:53:31.960 --> 00:53:33.484
[Seiji] No, of course not.

721
00:53:33.562 --> 00:53:35.894
We hold violin-making classes here.

722
00:53:35.964 --> 00:53:38.229
But one of them's yours, isn't it?

723
00:53:38.301 --> 00:53:41.293
- Yeah.
- So which one is it?

724
00:53:41.371 --> 00:53:44.169
- The end.
- Wow.

725
00:53:44.240 --> 00:53:45.765
That's really fantastic.

726
00:53:45.843 --> 00:53:48.471
I can't believe you can
make something like this.

727
00:53:48.546 --> 00:53:50.070
It's like magic, isn't it?

728
00:53:50.147 --> 00:53:51.809
You're so weird.

729
00:53:51.883 --> 00:53:55.148
I can't believe some of the stuff
that comes out of your mouth.

730
00:53:55.220 --> 00:53:58.247
It is magic. You made a violin
pop out of a piece of wood.

731
00:53:58.324 --> 00:54:00.724
Anyone can make a violin
of that caliber.

732
00:54:02.128 --> 00:54:04.323
I'm not close to being good enough.

733
00:54:10.671 --> 00:54:12.936
So, can you play the violin?

734
00:54:13.007 --> 00:54:14.133
Sort of.

735
00:54:14.209 --> 00:54:17.007
Would you play something for me,
just a little bit?

736
00:54:17.078 --> 00:54:18.137
Give me a break.

737
00:54:18.214 --> 00:54:20.614
Come on, come on. Won't you, please?

738
00:54:20.683 --> 00:54:23.208
All right, but you're
gonna have to sing along.

739
00:54:23.285 --> 00:54:24.878
What?

740
00:54:24.955 --> 00:54:27.480
You don't want me to sing. I'm terrible.

741
00:54:27.557 --> 00:54:29.821
I've got just the song for you.

742
00:54:44.844 --> 00:54:47.836
Are you ready?
I'm pretty sure you know this one.

743
00:54:48.782 --> 00:54:51.775
[♪ Take Me Home, Country Roads]

744
00:55:08.671 --> 00:55:10.936
[Tapping foot in rhythm]

745
00:55:11.742 --> 00:55:14.336
♪ I dreamed of living

746
00:55:14.411 --> 00:55:17.404
♪ Alone but fearless

747
00:55:17.482 --> 00:55:19.950
♪ Secret longing

748
00:55:20.018 --> 00:55:23.010
♪ To be courageous

749
00:55:23.087 --> 00:55:25.283
♪ Loneliness kept

750
00:55:25.357 --> 00:55:27.951
♪ Bottled up inside

751
00:55:28.027 --> 00:55:30.496
♪ Just reveal your brave face

752
00:55:30.564 --> 00:55:33.158
♪ They'll never know you lied

753
00:55:33.233 --> 00:55:35.428
♪ Country road

754
00:55:35.502 --> 00:55:38.097
♪ May lead me home

755
00:55:38.172 --> 00:55:41.039
♪ Know I belong there

756
00:55:41.108 --> 00:55:43.976
♪ All on my own

757
00:55:44.046 --> 00:55:46.913
- ♪ Destiny calls
- Shh!

758
00:55:46.982 --> 00:55:49.542
♪ Motionless, I stall

759
00:55:49.618 --> 00:55:52.247
♪ Know I can't go

760
00:55:52.322 --> 00:55:54.847
♪ Country road

761
00:55:56.192 --> 00:55:59.390
♪ No matter how dark
the world's inside me

762
00:55:59.463 --> 00:56:01.522
[tambourine rattling]

763
00:56:01.599 --> 00:56:05.593
♪ I'll never stop to show a tear
that I've shed

764
00:56:05.670 --> 00:56:09.869
- [accompanying instruments playing]
- ♪ But now I have to walk so fast

765
00:56:09.942 --> 00:56:12.502
♪ Running sprinting to forget

766
00:56:12.578 --> 00:56:17.107
♪ What is lodged in my head

767
00:56:17.184 --> 00:56:19.812
♪ Country road

768
00:56:19.887 --> 00:56:22.754
♪ May lead me home

769
00:56:22.823 --> 00:56:25.315
♪ Know I belong there

770
00:56:25.393 --> 00:56:28.487
♪ All on my own

771
00:56:28.563 --> 00:56:30.964
♪ Destiny calls

772
00:56:31.033 --> 00:56:34.093
♪ Motionless, I stall

773
00:56:34.169 --> 00:56:36.832
♪ Know I can't go

774
00:56:36.907 --> 00:56:39.535
♪ Country road

775
00:56:39.609 --> 00:56:42.237
[all] ♪ Country road

776
00:56:42.312 --> 00:56:45.180
[men] ♪ La la la la

777
00:56:45.249 --> 00:56:50.711
♪ You're a good friend
I'll never know

778
00:56:50.789 --> 00:56:53.314
♪ Same tomorrow

779
00:56:53.392 --> 00:56:56.123
♪ Regret and sorrow

780
00:56:56.195 --> 00:56:58.993
♪ Can't take you home

781
00:56:59.065 --> 00:57:02.627
[playing a fill]

782
00:57:02.703 --> 00:57:05.831
♪ Country road ♪

783
00:57:34.105 --> 00:57:37.269
- [laughing]
- [Clapping]

784
00:57:37.343 --> 00:57:39.140
That was wonderful, you two.

785
00:57:41.513 --> 00:57:45.041
I'm Shizuku, by the way.
Thanks for the great accompaniment.

786
00:57:47.320 --> 00:57:48.982
You're welcome, Shizuku.

787
00:57:49.056 --> 00:57:51.456
I was hoping we would meet up again.

788
00:57:51.525 --> 00:57:54.221
These are my good friends,
Kita and Minami.

789
00:57:54.295 --> 00:57:56.287
Nice vocals.

790
00:57:56.365 --> 00:58:00.233
You're the lucky girl who got to see
the grandfather clock strike 12:00.

791
00:58:00.302 --> 00:58:03.534
I never knew you had
such a pretty friend, Seiji.

792
00:58:03.606 --> 00:58:05.938
What? Seiji?

793
00:58:06.009 --> 00:58:08.307
Is your name Seiji Amasawa?

794
00:58:08.378 --> 00:58:10.279
Yeah. Of course.

795
00:58:10.347 --> 00:58:13.282
- Wait, didn't I tell you my name?
- No, you didn't.

796
00:58:13.350 --> 00:58:16.286
I thought it was Nishi.
That's what's on the sign.

797
00:58:16.354 --> 00:58:19.551
That's my grandfather's last name.
Mine is Amasawa.

798
00:58:19.624 --> 00:58:23.493
[Groaning] This is my worst nightmare.
I should have known better.

799
00:58:23.562 --> 00:58:26.861
- I never get the fairy tale ending.
- What are you babbling about?

800
00:58:26.932 --> 00:58:29.231
What difference does it make
what my name is?

801
00:58:29.302 --> 00:58:32.863
It makes a difference! You knew
my name but you never told me yours.

802
00:58:32.939 --> 00:58:35.033
[Seiji] You could've asked me my name.

803
00:58:35.109 --> 00:58:37.771
[Shizuku] I never had a chance!
This is so unfair!

804
00:58:37.845 --> 00:58:41.246
- I was so sure Seiji Amasawa was...
- I was what?

805
00:58:41.315 --> 00:58:43.648
A nice, intelligent, civilized person.

806
00:58:43.719 --> 00:58:45.880
Oh, really?
You read too many fairy tales.

807
00:58:45.954 --> 00:58:48.685
[Shizuku] Clearly you've read
a lot of them yourself.

808
00:58:48.758 --> 00:58:50.919
[Laughing]

809
00:58:53.329 --> 00:58:56.390
[Bicycle spokes clicking]

810
00:59:04.009 --> 00:59:07.604
Your grandpa and his friends
are really nice. I had a great time.

811
00:59:07.679 --> 00:59:11.172
You'll have to come back.
Grandpa and his friends would like that.

812
00:59:11.250 --> 00:59:14.550
Next time I'm keeping my mouth shut.
No yelling or singing.

813
00:59:14.621 --> 00:59:16.919
I could listen
to you play violin for hours.

814
00:59:16.990 --> 00:59:21.291
- Have you ever thought of performing?
- My violin playing's nothing special.

815
00:59:21.362 --> 00:59:24.058
My ultimate goal
is to be a world-class violin maker.

816
00:59:24.132 --> 00:59:27.067
That's great.
You're already so good at it.

817
00:59:27.135 --> 00:59:29.070
No, if you really want to be good

818
00:59:29.138 --> 00:59:31.629
you have to be trained
in Cremona, Italy.

819
00:59:31.707 --> 00:59:34.643
I want to go there
when I graduate from junior high.

820
00:59:34.711 --> 00:59:36.576
You're not going to high school?

821
00:59:36.646 --> 00:59:38.238
My parents think I am,

822
00:59:38.315 --> 00:59:41.251
but my grandpa is trying
to convince them otherwise.

823
00:59:41.319 --> 00:59:43.947
I guess we'll have to see.
Cross your fingers.

824
00:59:55.602 --> 00:59:58.867
That's great that you know what
you want to do with your life.

825
00:59:58.938 --> 01:00:01.407
I don't have a clue
what I want to do with mine.

826
01:00:01.475 --> 01:00:03.500
I just waste time writing corny lyrics.

827
01:00:03.577 --> 01:00:07.069
I know what I want to do,
but I don't know if I'll get to do it.

828
01:00:07.149 --> 01:00:09.549
I fight with my parents
about it everyday.

829
01:00:09.618 --> 01:00:12.883
Even if I get to go, it doesn't mean
that I'll be any good at it.

830
01:00:12.954 --> 01:00:15.219
I'll just have
to do my best and find out.

831
01:00:17.360 --> 01:00:19.294
You sure you don't want a ride home?

832
01:00:19.362 --> 01:00:21.297
Yeah. It's just around the corner.

833
01:00:21.365 --> 01:00:23.026
See ya.

834
01:00:23.100 --> 01:00:24.863
Uh, Shizuku...

835
01:00:24.935 --> 01:00:27.166
[gasping] Yeah?

836
01:00:27.238 --> 01:00:30.139
I just wanted to say
that I actually liked your lyrics.

837
01:00:30.208 --> 01:00:34.043
You're a very talented writer. Keep
pursuing it. It's not a waste of time.

838
01:00:34.113 --> 01:00:37.378
Just the other day
you told me my lyrics were corny.

839
01:00:37.449 --> 01:00:40.043
- Oh, did I really say that?
- Seiji!

840
01:00:40.120 --> 01:00:41.883
I'm sorry.

841
01:00:42.789 --> 01:00:46.122
Ha! You're forgetful too. See you later.

842
01:01:00.677 --> 01:01:03.339
[Footsteps approaching]

843
01:01:05.682 --> 01:01:09.551
Shizuku, turn off your lamp.
You left it on all night last night.

844
01:01:11.222 --> 01:01:14.158
[Creaking]

845
01:01:16.361 --> 01:01:19.421
When did you know
what to do with your life?

846
01:01:19.497 --> 01:01:22.194
- [Shiho] What are you talking about?
- You know!

847
01:01:22.268 --> 01:01:24.668
Don't worry about it.
You'll take your exams

848
01:01:24.737 --> 01:01:28.504
and whatever high school you get into
will pretty much decide things.

849
01:01:28.575 --> 01:01:31.772
- [Shizuku] Don't we get a choice?
- You do if you study hard.

850
01:01:31.845 --> 01:01:33.438
- [Sighing]
- Now go to sleep.

851
01:01:33.514 --> 01:01:35.106
Good night.

852
01:01:45.628 --> 01:01:48.655
- [Rain pattering]
- [Panting]

853
01:01:48.732 --> 01:01:53.295
I can't believe Mom didn't wake me up.
She's getting more forgetful than I am.

854
01:01:55.006 --> 01:01:57.065
[Panting]

855
01:02:02.214 --> 01:02:05.342
- Uh, hello?
- Oh, hello.

856
01:02:05.417 --> 01:02:07.215
Can't you run any faster?

857
01:02:07.287 --> 01:02:09.482
You don't have to wait for me.

858
01:02:12.426 --> 01:02:14.894
[Shizuku panting]

859
01:02:18.299 --> 01:02:20.530
[Bell chiming]

860
01:02:20.602 --> 01:02:23.696
[Students talking, giggling]

861
01:02:25.708 --> 01:02:28.438
[Sighing] Just made it.

862
01:02:28.511 --> 01:02:30.706
Shizuku, what happened?

863
01:02:30.780 --> 01:02:32.373
Ah, you look like a wreck.

864
01:02:32.449 --> 01:02:35.179
Well, you seem fine.
You sure do recover fast.

865
01:02:35.252 --> 01:02:38.780
Is it true that you were out with a boy
from another class last night?

866
01:02:38.856 --> 01:02:41.222
- Where did you hear that?
- It's a rumor.

867
01:02:41.292 --> 01:02:44.193
They say it looked like
the two of you are going steady.

868
01:02:44.262 --> 01:02:47.232
- It's nothing like that, Yuko.
- I'm not worried about it.

869
01:02:51.403 --> 01:02:53.065
[Boy] It's what the book says.

870
01:02:53.139 --> 01:02:54.868
Yuko, about my friend's letter,

871
01:02:54.941 --> 01:02:57.933
I'll tell my friend you're not
interested. I'm sorry.

872
01:02:58.011 --> 01:03:00.071
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

873
01:03:00.147 --> 01:03:01.944
It's OK.

874
01:03:06.388 --> 01:03:10.654
Hey, did you see Sasuke last night?
I was blown away. It was the best ever!

875
01:03:13.629 --> 01:03:16.621
[Bell chiming]

876
01:03:17.266 --> 01:03:20.065
This formula's gonna be
on tomorrow's test, class,

877
01:03:20.137 --> 01:03:22.833
- so make sure you know it.
- [Groaning]

878
01:03:22.906 --> 01:03:24.464
[Teacher] Class dismissed.

879
01:03:25.577 --> 01:03:28.512
- [Laughing]
- You forgot your books.

880
01:03:30.048 --> 01:03:33.143
[Boy] I'm a little nervous
to ask her out. I mean, should I?

881
01:03:33.219 --> 01:03:35.084
[Girl] I didn't even get to see it.

882
01:03:35.154 --> 01:03:37.622
No way! [laughing]

883
01:03:42.796 --> 01:03:44.856
[Laughing]

884
01:03:44.932 --> 01:03:47.264
Excuse me, is this Shizuku's classroom?

885
01:03:48.002 --> 01:03:49.765
Hey, Amasawa, what's up?

886
01:03:49.837 --> 01:03:52.272
I'm looking for Shizuku. Is she in here?

887
01:03:52.341 --> 01:03:55.708
Shizuku? Yeah, she's here.

888
01:03:55.778 --> 01:03:59.442
Hey Shizuku, you got a visitor.
It's a guy!

889
01:03:59.516 --> 01:04:01.040
[Talking stops]

890
01:04:03.686 --> 01:04:06.815
- Seiji, she's right over there.
- [Chuckling]

891
01:04:06.891 --> 01:04:09.587
[Gasping] Hi, Seiji.

892
01:04:09.660 --> 01:04:12.152
Shizuku, can we talk for a minute?

893
01:04:12.230 --> 01:04:14.289
Uh, sure.

894
01:04:14.366 --> 01:04:16.857
[Boy] Check it out!
Shizuku's got a boyfriend!

895
01:04:16.935 --> 01:04:18.665
[Cheering]

896
01:04:18.738 --> 01:04:20.467
♪ Shizuku's got a boyfriend ♪

897
01:04:20.540 --> 01:04:23.634
No, I don't.
Hey, he's not my boyfriend!

898
01:04:23.709 --> 01:04:26.304
- [Laughing]
- [Girl] Aww, come on.

899
01:04:26.380 --> 01:04:28.041
Boyfri... [grunting]

900
01:04:30.317 --> 01:04:31.979
All right, what is it?

901
01:04:32.053 --> 01:04:34.851
I get to go to Cremona, Italy.
I just found out.

902
01:04:34.923 --> 01:04:37.255
What? Come on, let's go.

903
01:04:37.325 --> 01:04:40.454
[Laughing, cheering]

904
01:04:42.131 --> 01:04:44.464
- Where are we going?
- To the roof.

905
01:04:47.804 --> 01:04:49.328
[Groaning]

906
01:04:51.742 --> 01:04:53.835
Oh, excellent.

907
01:04:53.911 --> 01:04:58.679
Seiji, why did you broadcast to the
class that you wanted to talk to me?

908
01:04:58.750 --> 01:05:02.151
I'm sorry. I was excited and
I wanted you to be the first to know.

909
01:05:04.491 --> 01:05:08.120
But now people might get
the idea that you like me.

910
01:05:08.194 --> 01:05:10.025
Don't worry about it.

911
01:05:10.096 --> 01:05:13.032
Hey, so even though my parents
gave in there's a catch.

912
01:05:13.100 --> 01:05:14.362
Oh. What's the catch?

913
01:05:14.435 --> 01:05:15.902
Well, when I'm in Italy

914
01:05:15.970 --> 01:05:19.839
I have to try out with this friend of
my grandpa's who owns the workshop.

915
01:05:19.908 --> 01:05:21.307
Try out?

916
01:05:21.376 --> 01:05:24.278
Yeah, my parents said
I get two months to prove myself.

917
01:05:24.347 --> 01:05:27.316
If my grandpa's friend
doesn't think I have potential,

918
01:05:27.383 --> 01:05:30.376
then I have to come back here
and go to high school.

919
01:05:30.454 --> 01:05:33.514
I've heard this guy is really tough
on his apprentices,

920
01:05:33.590 --> 01:05:37.391
so it doesn't seem fair that my parents
are only giving me one shot.

921
01:05:37.462 --> 01:05:39.794
But it's a great opportunity,
so I'm going.

922
01:05:39.864 --> 01:05:43.197
- When? Do you leave soon?
- As soon as I get my passport.

923
01:05:43.268 --> 01:05:45.897
My dad said he was going
to notify the school today.

924
01:05:45.971 --> 01:05:48.166
Wow, that fast, huh?

925
01:05:49.341 --> 01:05:51.810
I'm happy for you.
Your dream's coming true.

926
01:05:51.878 --> 01:05:54.813
I hope so. I'm going
to give it everything I've got.

927
01:05:57.418 --> 01:05:58.817
- Would you?
- Oh...

928
01:06:00.755 --> 01:06:02.746
Hey, it stopped raining. Look.

929
01:06:02.823 --> 01:06:03.950
Yeah, you're right.

930
01:06:04.626 --> 01:06:06.821
Wow! Look at that view.

931
01:06:11.834 --> 01:06:13.825
Maybe we'll see a rainbow.

932
01:06:13.903 --> 01:06:14.995
Yeah.

933
01:06:25.250 --> 01:06:28.117
I wonder what
Cremona, Italy will be like.

934
01:06:28.186 --> 01:06:30.155
I hope it turns out to be a nice place.

935
01:06:30.223 --> 01:06:32.851
Mm-hmm. The city's really old,

936
01:06:32.925 --> 01:06:35.917
and everybody there
thinks violin making is respectable.

937
01:06:35.995 --> 01:06:37.395
That's great.

938
01:06:37.464 --> 01:06:40.399
It's so brave of you to go
after your dream like that.

939
01:06:40.467 --> 01:06:42.435
I just waste my time reading books,

940
01:06:42.502 --> 01:06:46.667
and all I've been dreaming about was
we would go to the same high school.

941
01:06:46.741 --> 01:06:50.473
[Chuckling] OK, that was embarrassing.
I shouldn't have said that.

942
01:06:52.982 --> 01:06:54.882
- Shh! Stay down.
- [Giggling]

943
01:06:54.950 --> 01:06:57.442
- Do you think they'll kiss?
- [Boy] Hurry up.

944
01:07:07.431 --> 01:07:10.230
You know, I noticed you a long time ago.

945
01:07:10.302 --> 01:07:12.634
I first spotted you
reading in the library.

946
01:07:12.704 --> 01:07:17.108
I walked past you hundreds of times,
but you never noticed me, right?

947
01:07:17.176 --> 01:07:20.236
I even sat down in the chair
right next to you a couple times.

948
01:07:20.313 --> 01:07:21.507
Yeah?

949
01:07:21.581 --> 01:07:24.050
Then I started checking out
all sorts of books

950
01:07:24.118 --> 01:07:26.609
just so I can get my name
on the cards before you.

951
01:07:26.687 --> 01:07:29.054
- Guess that got your attention.
- [Gasping]

952
01:07:29.124 --> 01:07:32.719
But now... I have to take off to Italy.

953
01:07:32.794 --> 01:07:35.821
That's some pretty lousy timing,
don't you think?

954
01:07:39.068 --> 01:07:41.059
Yeah, that's pretty bad.

955
01:07:42.004 --> 01:07:44.473
[Boy] Hey, quit pushin'! I can't see!

956
01:07:44.541 --> 01:07:47.408
- [Grunting]
- [Gasping]

957
01:07:47.477 --> 01:07:50.174
[Laughing]

958
01:07:51.282 --> 01:07:53.216
You jerks!

959
01:07:55.954 --> 01:07:58.946
[Boy] Get out of the way!
Shizuku is really mad!

960
01:07:59.024 --> 01:08:00.548
[Grunting]

961
01:08:02.162 --> 01:08:04.562
- [Sniffling]
- [Gasping]

962
01:08:07.233 --> 01:08:08.222
Hey!

963
01:08:15.844 --> 01:08:18.312
[Sighing]

964
01:08:34.331 --> 01:08:36.197
- Here, Dad.
- Thank you.

965
01:08:36.267 --> 01:08:39.464
- I'm going to Yuko's.
- Shizuku, is that all you're having?

966
01:08:40.538 --> 01:08:42.200
I'm not hungry.

967
01:08:44.710 --> 01:08:47.406
Pick up some milk
on your way home, OK?

968
01:08:47.480 --> 01:08:49.472
[Shizuku] I don't feel like it.

969
01:08:49.549 --> 01:08:52.541
- Hey, you're the one who drank it all.
- [Door closing]

970
01:08:52.619 --> 01:08:55.418
She's really been slacking off
these last few days.

971
01:08:55.490 --> 01:08:57.890
[Train bell ringing]

972
01:09:03.565 --> 01:09:05.226
[Man] Taxi!

973
01:09:06.835 --> 01:09:08.770
[Woman] Sorry, I can't go.

974
01:09:15.179 --> 01:09:18.239
- Thanks for meeting me, Yuko.
- No problem.

975
01:09:18.315 --> 01:09:20.442
I've never been so confused in my life.

976
01:09:20.518 --> 01:09:22.043
[Yuko] Mom, Shizuku's here.

977
01:09:22.120 --> 01:09:26.079
- [Woman] Shizuku, how nice to see you.
- [Shizuku] Hi, Mrs. Harada.

978
01:09:26.158 --> 01:09:28.320
- [TVplays]
- Hello, girls.

979
01:09:28.394 --> 01:09:30.862
- Hi, Mr. Harada.
- Hi, Shizuku.

980
01:09:30.930 --> 01:09:33.398
Would you two like
some tea and cookies?

981
01:09:33.466 --> 01:09:35.128
[Yuko] Yeah. Thanks, Mom.

982
01:09:35.202 --> 01:09:38.399
I'm having a fight with my father.
I'm not talking to him.

983
01:09:44.612 --> 01:09:47.480
Boys really have guts, don't they?

984
01:09:48.551 --> 01:09:50.109
He'll be gone for two months.

985
01:09:50.186 --> 01:09:52.654
He's returning
for our graduation ceremony,

986
01:09:52.721 --> 01:09:55.816
then he's going back again
to study for about ten years.

987
01:09:55.892 --> 01:09:58.053
You'll practically never see him again.

988
01:09:58.128 --> 01:09:59.254
But you're so lucky.

989
01:09:59.329 --> 01:10:02.527
The two of you sound like
the perfect match, like soulmates.

990
01:10:02.600 --> 01:10:05.194
He's so much better than me.
We read the same books

991
01:10:05.269 --> 01:10:07.465
but I never do anything
with what I learn.

992
01:10:07.539 --> 01:10:09.632
He decided long ago
what he wanted to do.

993
01:10:09.708 --> 01:10:12.370
- He's going straight for his dream.
- I guess so.

994
01:10:13.612 --> 01:10:17.105
You know what? Kinuyo was in
the same first year class as Seiji.

995
01:10:17.183 --> 01:10:20.312
She said he was a little hard
to approach but a good student

996
01:10:20.387 --> 01:10:21.752
and really handsome too.

997
01:10:21.822 --> 01:10:23.653
You don't need to rub it in.

998
01:10:23.724 --> 01:10:25.988
I already feel like
I'm not good enough.

999
01:10:26.060 --> 01:10:27.756
This whole thing is doomed.

1000
01:10:27.829 --> 01:10:30.354
No, it's not.
All that matters is he likes you.

1001
01:10:30.432 --> 01:10:32.730
- Didn't he say that?
- Yeah.

1002
01:10:32.801 --> 01:10:34.997
But I'm not sure I believe it.

1003
01:10:35.071 --> 01:10:38.131
[Sighing] I don't get you.

1004
01:10:38.207 --> 01:10:40.472
It's so cool.
You could be writing letters

1005
01:10:40.544 --> 01:10:43.479
and encouraging
each other every single day.

1006
01:10:43.547 --> 01:10:45.538
How could I ever encourage him?

1007
01:10:45.616 --> 01:10:48.017
He's worked so much harder
than I ever have.

1008
01:10:48.086 --> 01:10:49.678
You are weird.

1009
01:10:50.555 --> 01:10:52.386
Just because you haven't decided

1010
01:10:52.457 --> 01:10:56.019
what you're going to do after you
graduate from junior high school

1011
01:10:56.095 --> 01:10:58.757
doesn't mean that you're not
good enough for him.

1012
01:10:58.831 --> 01:11:00.026
[Sighing]

1013
01:11:00.100 --> 01:11:02.534
Everyone in school
thinks you're talented.

1014
01:11:02.602 --> 01:11:06.299
You've read more books than anyone
I know and your lyrics are great.

1015
01:11:06.373 --> 01:11:09.639
And you can tell people just
what you feel. I can't do that.

1016
01:11:09.710 --> 01:11:11.644
[Sighing]

1017
01:11:11.712 --> 01:11:13.977
I'm not close to being good enough.

1018
01:11:14.049 --> 01:11:15.516
- Yes, you are.
- Mm-mmm.

1019
01:11:15.584 --> 01:11:16.983
That's what Seiji said.

1020
01:11:17.052 --> 01:11:19.316
He isn't sure he has any talent either.

1021
01:11:19.388 --> 01:11:21.584
I should test myself like he is.

1022
01:11:23.259 --> 01:11:26.388
That's what I'll do.
I'll try being a writer.

1023
01:11:26.463 --> 01:11:27.862
I've already got a story.

1024
01:11:27.932 --> 01:11:30.127
I've got two months
to see what I can do.

1025
01:11:30.868 --> 01:11:32.665
But midterms are coming up.

1026
01:11:32.736 --> 01:11:35.001
That's OK. Thanks, Yuko.

1027
01:11:35.073 --> 01:11:37.337
I feel like maybe
I can handle this now.

1028
01:11:37.409 --> 01:11:40.072
- You're going?
- Yeah. I've gotta get writing.

1029
01:11:41.614 --> 01:11:43.741
- [Barking]
- Bye, Mr. And Mrs. Harada.

1030
01:11:43.816 --> 01:11:46.047
- Bye, Sumo.
- Say hello to your mom for me.

1031
01:11:46.119 --> 01:11:47.484
[Shizuku] I will.

1032
01:11:49.957 --> 01:11:53.086
- You hang in there too, Yuko.
- Mm-hmm.

1033
01:11:53.161 --> 01:11:56.324
I'm sure Sugimura will see
what a good person you are.

1034
01:11:57.632 --> 01:11:58.894
See you later.

1035
01:12:00.903 --> 01:12:02.768
So that's it. It's simple.

1036
01:12:02.838 --> 01:12:04.897
All I have to do
is give my writing a try.

1037
01:12:07.911 --> 01:12:10.243
[Gasping] Moon.

1038
01:12:13.351 --> 01:12:16.013
[Girl] Muta! Muta!

1039
01:12:16.087 --> 01:12:19.524
Hey, Mom, Muta ran off again.

1040
01:12:19.591 --> 01:12:21.786
Where does he keep going?

1041
01:12:21.860 --> 01:12:23.657
Muta. Huh.

1042
01:12:26.933 --> 01:12:31.529
Whisper of the Heart
by Shizuku Tsukishima.

1043
01:12:31.604 --> 01:12:33.732
"Listen to the voice of the forest

1044
01:12:33.807 --> 01:12:37.800
and the wind that blows
from a far-off cluster of stars."

1045
01:12:56.066 --> 01:12:59.400
[Nishi] So, you want to write
a story about the Baron?

1046
01:12:59.470 --> 01:13:01.563
Something about him inspires me,

1047
01:13:01.639 --> 01:13:04.199
but I know the Baron
has special meaning for you,

1048
01:13:04.275 --> 01:13:08.042
so I thought I'd better ask your
permission before I use him in my book.

1049
01:13:08.113 --> 01:13:10.411
[Laughing] You can use the Baron.

1050
01:13:10.482 --> 01:13:12.542
Thank you for asking,

1051
01:13:12.619 --> 01:13:14.712
but I'd like to ask
for a favor in return.

1052
01:13:15.989 --> 01:13:17.456
Yes?

1053
01:13:17.524 --> 01:13:22.428
Once you have finished your story
I want to be the first to read it, hmm?

1054
01:13:22.496 --> 01:13:24.931
Oh, uh... I...

1055
01:13:25.000 --> 01:13:26.467
[Nishi] Is it a deal?

1056
01:13:26.535 --> 01:13:28.264
Do I really have to show it to you?

1057
01:13:28.336 --> 01:13:31.704
I've never written anything before.
I'm afraid it's gonna stink.

1058
01:13:31.774 --> 01:13:34.265
[Laughing]

1059
01:13:34.343 --> 01:13:37.335
You sound just like all
the other artists that I've met.

1060
01:13:37.413 --> 01:13:40.941
No one should expect perfection
when they're first starting out.

1061
01:13:41.018 --> 01:13:43.782
Wait a minute.
I've got something to show you.

1062
01:13:49.694 --> 01:13:52.095
I think you'll like this.

1063
01:13:55.568 --> 01:13:57.035
Take a look.

1064
01:14:01.641 --> 01:14:04.611
[Shizuku] It looks like a rock.

1065
01:14:04.679 --> 01:14:08.171
It's a special kind of rock
called a geode.

1066
01:14:08.249 --> 01:14:10.581
Hold it close to your eye
and look inside.

1067
01:14:10.651 --> 01:14:12.449
That's right, like that.

1068
01:14:20.597 --> 01:14:22.462
Wow.

1069
01:14:23.733 --> 01:14:25.031
Look at that.

1070
01:14:25.102 --> 01:14:27.263
Those crystals are called beryl.

1071
01:14:27.338 --> 01:14:30.535
There are pieces
of raw emeralds deep inside them.

1072
01:14:30.608 --> 01:14:33.544
- Aren't emeralds worth a lot of money?
- Sure.

1073
01:14:33.612 --> 01:14:37.207
But they need
to be cut and polished first.

1074
01:14:37.282 --> 01:14:40.548
When you first become an artist
you are like that rock.

1075
01:14:40.620 --> 01:14:44.057
You're in a raw natural state
with hidden gems inside.

1076
01:14:44.124 --> 01:14:49.027
You have to dig down deep and find
the emeralds tucked away inside you.

1077
01:14:50.063 --> 01:14:51.759
And that's just the beginning.

1078
01:14:51.833 --> 01:14:54.700
Once you've found your gems
you have to polish them.

1079
01:14:54.769 --> 01:14:57.033
It takes a lot of hard work.

1080
01:14:57.105 --> 01:15:01.304
Oh, and here's the tricky part:
Look at the crack in the geode.

1081
01:15:01.377 --> 01:15:02.571
OK.

1082
01:15:02.645 --> 01:15:04.978
You see that big green crystal there?

1083
01:15:05.048 --> 01:15:07.312
You could spend years polishing that

1084
01:15:07.384 --> 01:15:09.909
and it wouldn't be worth much at all.

1085
01:15:09.986 --> 01:15:12.512
The smaller crystals
are much more valuable,

1086
01:15:12.590 --> 01:15:15.525
and there may be some even
deeper inside that we can't see

1087
01:15:15.593 --> 01:15:17.323
which are even more precious.

1088
01:15:17.396 --> 01:15:20.923
[Chuckling] Oh, it's bad to get old.
You just keep rambling.

1089
01:15:20.999 --> 01:15:22.466
I'll shut up now.

1090
01:15:23.870 --> 01:15:26.737
What if I look inside myself
and I don't find any gems?

1091
01:15:26.806 --> 01:15:28.535
What if I'm just a rock?

1092
01:15:28.608 --> 01:15:30.132
I'm going to try anyway.

1093
01:15:30.211 --> 01:15:33.476
I'll write that story and I'll
let you be the first to read it.

1094
01:15:33.547 --> 01:15:36.516
That's the spirit.
I'll be looking forward to it.

1095
01:15:44.026 --> 01:15:48.486
A raw gem in a vein of lapis lazuli.

1096
01:15:52.169 --> 01:15:54.501
Ah, let us go forth together,

1097
01:15:54.571 --> 01:15:57.769
in search of the vein of lapis lazuli.

1098
01:15:59.577 --> 01:16:01.238
Look. Be not fearful.

1099
01:16:01.312 --> 01:16:04.771
On the day of the new moon
space is warped.

1100
01:16:07.253 --> 01:16:10.781
[Baron] As such,
things far away loom large

1101
01:16:10.857 --> 01:16:13.951
whereas things near at hand
appear small.

1102
01:16:14.027 --> 01:16:15.790
Come, let us fly.

1103
01:16:15.862 --> 01:16:18.331
We will rise on the updraft!

1104
01:16:22.837 --> 01:16:24.533
But we must hurry!

1105
01:16:24.606 --> 01:16:26.972
Quick! The planetoids are gathering.

1106
01:16:28.677 --> 01:16:30.009
Shall we?

1107
01:16:30.079 --> 01:16:32.513
And... off we go!

1108
01:16:32.582 --> 01:16:35.449
[Shizuku screaming]

1109
01:16:38.923 --> 01:16:41.756
That's it!
We're riding the air currents.

1110
01:16:41.825 --> 01:16:44.852
See that tower?
We'll clear it in a single leap.

1111
01:16:44.930 --> 01:16:47.228
[Shizuku] Are you kidding?
That's so high.

1112
01:16:47.299 --> 01:16:49.495
[Baron] Ah, it just looks high.

1113
01:16:49.568 --> 01:16:52.560
You'll see once we get closer.

1114
01:17:08.690 --> 01:17:11.717
Let's go. When the
afternoon air currents mix,

1115
01:17:11.794 --> 01:17:13.853
we can even touch
the stars without fear.

1116
01:17:15.597 --> 01:17:16.690
That's strange.

1117
01:17:20.470 --> 01:17:22.735
Shizuku's in nonfiction?

1118
01:17:22.807 --> 01:17:25.935
I've never seen her look
at anything but fairy tales.

1119
01:18:04.521 --> 01:18:08.515
It's a prisoner locked in a cell
and he's making a violin.

1120
01:18:35.023 --> 01:18:37.014
[Gasping]

1121
01:18:40.896 --> 01:18:43.161
Seiji! [gasping]

1122
01:18:43.232 --> 01:18:45.359
I thought you had left for Italy.

1123
01:18:45.435 --> 01:18:48.735
I just talked to my grandpa.
He said you might be here.

1124
01:18:48.806 --> 01:18:52.469
I'm glad I found you.
I'm leaving tomorrow.

1125
01:18:52.543 --> 01:18:54.535
You are?

1126
01:18:55.980 --> 01:18:58.847
Go on. You should keep working.

1127
01:18:58.917 --> 01:19:00.782
I'll wait until you're done.

1128
01:19:26.682 --> 01:19:28.674
Sorry I can't see you home.

1129
01:19:29.552 --> 01:19:32.214
I'm just glad I was able
to see you again.

1130
01:19:32.288 --> 01:19:34.223
I can't go to the airport with you

1131
01:19:34.291 --> 01:19:36.759
but I'll be waiting for you
when you come back.

1132
01:19:36.827 --> 01:19:38.556
I'll see you in two months then.

1133
01:19:45.036 --> 01:19:48.700
I'm sorry for complaining
all the time, Seiji.

1134
01:19:48.774 --> 01:19:51.402
I promise I'll work hard
while you're gone.

1135
01:19:58.051 --> 01:20:00.110
Well, I better go.

1136
01:20:03.124 --> 01:20:04.591
Have a safe trip.

1137
01:20:22.813 --> 01:20:25.680
Louise, my betrothed and I,

1138
01:20:25.750 --> 01:20:28.743
were born in a far-off land.

1139
01:20:33.025 --> 01:20:37.087
[Baron] Back then,
magic was still alive in our town,

1140
01:20:37.163 --> 01:20:39.688
and the streets
were lined with shops

1141
01:20:39.766 --> 01:20:43.760
where the descendents of magicians
worked as artisans.

1142
01:20:47.509 --> 01:20:52.378
The craftsman who made us
was a poor apprentice dollmaker.

1143
01:20:55.651 --> 01:20:58.518
But Louise and I were happy,

1144
01:20:58.588 --> 01:21:00.580
for the man who made us

1145
01:21:00.657 --> 01:21:03.592
gave us the ability to love.

1146
01:21:03.994 --> 01:21:07.123
Then one day...

1147
01:21:12.604 --> 01:21:14.470
[Yuko] Shizuku.

1148
01:21:14.540 --> 01:21:16.303
Shizuku!

1149
01:21:17.076 --> 01:21:18.737
- Shizuku!
- [Gasping]

1150
01:21:19.846 --> 01:21:22.610
The answer, Shizuku?

1151
01:21:22.682 --> 01:21:24.673
Stand up.

1152
01:21:24.751 --> 01:21:27.414
I don't know, sir.
I wasn't paying attention.

1153
01:21:27.488 --> 01:21:30.423
[Teacher] You haven't
been paying attention all week.

1154
01:21:30.491 --> 01:21:33.256
- I'm sorry, sir.
- Yuko, will you help out Shizuku?

1155
01:21:33.328 --> 01:21:35.523
Yes, sir.

1156
01:21:35.597 --> 01:21:38.828
What? You were up
until four in the morning?

1157
01:21:38.900 --> 01:21:41.563
I just can't seem to stop writing
for some reason.

1158
01:21:42.572 --> 01:21:46.566
You keep spacing out
all the time, like today.

1159
01:21:46.644 --> 01:21:48.441
I was thinking about my story.

1160
01:21:48.512 --> 01:21:51.572
There's so much I want to write.
I can't find enough time.

1161
01:21:51.649 --> 01:21:55.108
[Sighing] I don't feel like eating.

1162
01:21:56.721 --> 01:21:58.746
[Squeaking]

1163
01:22:04.730 --> 01:22:07.063
[Shuffling foot]

1164
01:22:17.278 --> 01:22:18.745
[Shuffling foot]

1165
01:22:18.813 --> 01:22:21.612
- [Door opening]
- [Footsteps]

1166
01:22:23.886 --> 01:22:26.481
[Mom] Oh! Shizuku, it's you.

1167
01:22:26.556 --> 01:22:28.353
You scared me half to death.

1168
01:22:28.425 --> 01:22:30.290
Why didn't you have the lights on?

1169
01:22:30.360 --> 01:22:32.761
Oh, Shizuku,
you didn't finish the laundry.

1170
01:22:32.830 --> 01:22:35.424
Get in here, Shizuku! Shizuku!

1171
01:22:38.636 --> 01:22:42.300
[Slurping] Where's Shizuku?
Doesn't she want dinner?

1172
01:22:42.374 --> 01:22:44.365
She said she isn't hungry.

1173
01:23:03.865 --> 01:23:06.334
- [Girls laughing]
- Can you believe that?

1174
01:23:06.402 --> 01:23:07.801
She actually said that.

1175
01:23:09.071 --> 01:23:10.800
Oh, hello, Mrs. Tsukishima.

1176
01:23:10.873 --> 01:23:13.468
- Sorry to keep you waiting.
- No trouble at all.

1177
01:23:13.543 --> 01:23:16.171
Do you know if the career
counseling room is open?

1178
01:23:16.246 --> 01:23:18.340
- Yeah.
- Come this way.

1179
01:23:24.822 --> 01:23:26.154
[Mom] I'm home.

1180
01:23:28.827 --> 01:23:30.226
Hi there, Mom.

1181
01:23:30.996 --> 01:23:33.431
You're home early today.

1182
01:23:34.567 --> 01:23:36.831
Ohh, I'm exhausted.

1183
01:23:36.903 --> 01:23:39.566
- Want some coffee?
- Sounds great.

1184
01:23:42.176 --> 01:23:45.305
So, Mom, there's something
I need to talk to you about.

1185
01:23:45.380 --> 01:23:48.838
[Mom] Not something bad, I hope.
I already have a headache.

1186
01:23:51.854 --> 01:23:54.288
I'm thinking of moving
into my own place.

1187
01:23:54.357 --> 01:23:56.587
[Shiho] I found the greatest apartment.

1188
01:23:56.659 --> 01:23:58.821
Honey, can you really
afford to move out?

1189
01:23:58.896 --> 01:24:01.797
I saved some money from my temp job,

1190
01:24:01.865 --> 01:24:05.597
and I just got a part-time position
in a test-preparation school.

1191
01:24:05.670 --> 01:24:10.073
I see. I've gotten so used to you
helping me out while I'm in school.

1192
01:24:10.141 --> 01:24:13.202
But we'll be fine.
I'll talk to your father about it.

1193
01:24:13.279 --> 01:24:15.611
Really? Thanks, Mom.

1194
01:24:17.349 --> 01:24:20.183
Financially I think you'll
have to manage on your own

1195
01:24:20.253 --> 01:24:22.483
until I finish my last
semester of school.

1196
01:24:22.556 --> 01:24:25.754
- Once I graduate I can help you out.
- That'd be great.

1197
01:24:25.827 --> 01:24:29.627
I hate to do this now while you're in
the middle of your master's thesis.

1198
01:24:29.697 --> 01:24:30.892
Don't worry about it.

1199
01:24:30.966 --> 01:24:34.493
I really appreciate all the help
you gave me preparing the data.

1200
01:24:34.570 --> 01:24:36.936
It'll be good for Shizuku
to have her own room

1201
01:24:37.005 --> 01:24:40.772
so she can focus on her studies.
She's been acting so strange lately.

1202
01:24:40.844 --> 01:24:42.175
You're telling me.

1203
01:24:42.245 --> 01:24:46.307
I had a conference today with
one of her teachers. Look at this.

1204
01:24:46.383 --> 01:24:48.442
Huh. What is it?

1205
01:24:48.519 --> 01:24:50.647
[Gasping] What's happened to her?

1206
01:24:50.722 --> 01:24:52.713
I've never seen grades this low.

1207
01:24:53.658 --> 01:24:56.183
It's so strange.
I wonder what she's doing.

1208
01:24:56.261 --> 01:24:58.093
She's at her desk all day.

1209
01:25:05.873 --> 01:25:08.398
- Oh, good evening.
- Good evening.

1210
01:25:10.745 --> 01:25:12.269
Thank you.

1211
01:25:17.319 --> 01:25:21.016
[Shiho] With grades like that,
no high school will accept you.

1212
01:25:21.090 --> 01:25:24.151
[Shizuku] Fine. I'm not going
to high school anyway.

1213
01:25:24.227 --> 01:25:27.390
Are you crazy? You think
a junior high education is enough?

1214
01:25:27.464 --> 01:25:29.625
What kind of fantasy world
are you living in?

1215
01:25:29.699 --> 01:25:32.260
Hey, it's my future
so I make the decision.

1216
01:25:32.336 --> 01:25:36.740
Don't give me that attitude. You know
you're being completely ridiculous.

1217
01:25:36.808 --> 01:25:39.572
If you keep acting like this
you'll ruin your life.

1218
01:25:39.645 --> 01:25:41.670
School's really made your life great.

1219
01:25:41.747 --> 01:25:44.649
All you've done since college
is work part-time jobs.

1220
01:25:44.717 --> 01:25:47.185
[Shiho] I'm making money
and I can support myself.

1221
01:25:47.253 --> 01:25:49.619
What job will you get
without a college degree?

1222
01:25:49.689 --> 01:25:53.490
You'll end up destitute because
you're in some stupid rebellious phase.

1223
01:25:53.561 --> 01:25:56.793
[Shizuku] I'm not being rebellious.
I'm going after my dreams.

1224
01:25:56.865 --> 01:25:59.800
What dreams? You just
goof around reading books.

1225
01:25:59.868 --> 01:26:03.202
Stop the arguing, girls.
I've heard enough.

1226
01:26:03.272 --> 01:26:06.298
But Dad, she's gonna ruin her life
if she keeps this up.

1227
01:26:06.375 --> 01:26:09.834
Hmm. All right. Let's go
to the kitchen and discuss this.

1228
01:26:09.913 --> 01:26:12.973
Shizuku, change out
of your uniform first, please.

1229
01:26:15.152 --> 01:26:16.814
Hurry it up.

1230
01:26:30.170 --> 01:26:31.831
A bit low.

1231
01:26:31.905 --> 01:26:34.373
Shizuku, are you doing
the best you can?

1232
01:26:34.441 --> 01:26:36.501
Yes! I take these tests very seriously.

1233
01:26:36.577 --> 01:26:39.774
Just a little bit ago you said
you weren't going to high school.

1234
01:26:39.847 --> 01:26:42.715
You were the one who said
no high school would accept me.

1235
01:26:42.784 --> 01:26:44.911
Shiho, I'd like to talk
to Shizuku alone.

1236
01:26:44.987 --> 01:26:47.148
Would you please
excuse yourself, honey?

1237
01:26:47.222 --> 01:26:48.689
Fine.

1238
01:26:50.793 --> 01:26:53.591
- Where's your mother?
- She's at the Tanakas.

1239
01:26:53.663 --> 01:26:56.827
- [Mom] I'm home.
- [Shiho] There she is. Hey, Mom.

1240
01:26:56.900 --> 01:27:00.063
- [Mom] Is your father home?
- [Shiho] He's in the kitchen.

1241
01:27:00.137 --> 01:27:03.198
[Dad] Could you come in here?
I'm having a talk with Shizuku.

1242
01:27:03.274 --> 01:27:05.105
[Mom] Sure. Just a second.

1243
01:27:07.145 --> 01:27:08.737
[Door closing]

1244
01:27:10.683 --> 01:27:13.584
[Dad] All right, Shizuku.

1245
01:27:13.653 --> 01:27:15.952
You have something that you're doing

1246
01:27:16.023 --> 01:27:18.753
that you think is more important
than studying?

1247
01:27:20.827 --> 01:27:23.160
Will you tell us what it is?

1248
01:27:24.098 --> 01:27:26.225
When I can tell you, I will.

1249
01:27:26.300 --> 01:27:30.567
Shizuku, can't you do whatever it is
once your exams are over?

1250
01:27:30.639 --> 01:27:34.439
I have to do it now. I've only
got three weeks left before he...

1251
01:27:34.510 --> 01:27:38.572
It's that I promised myself
I'd achieve this certain goal

1252
01:27:38.648 --> 01:27:41.378
- or I'm not good enough.
- Good enough for what?

1253
01:27:41.451 --> 01:27:43.818
Why do you need to prove yourself?

1254
01:27:44.955 --> 01:27:48.049
[Mom] We can't help you
unless you tell us what's going on.

1255
01:27:48.125 --> 01:27:53.120
What could you be doing that you
can't tell your mother and father about?

1256
01:27:53.198 --> 01:27:57.135
- Honey, please.
- Oh, sorry. I'll put it out.

1257
01:27:59.272 --> 01:28:01.206
[Exhaling]

1258
01:28:06.213 --> 01:28:08.078
You work so hard in the library.

1259
01:28:08.148 --> 01:28:10.811
Whatever you're doing,
I know it's important to you.

1260
01:28:10.885 --> 01:28:13.752
And I truly respect that.

1261
01:28:13.822 --> 01:28:18.123
Honey, why don't we let Shizuku
do what she thinks is best?

1262
01:28:18.194 --> 01:28:20.685
Not everyone needs
to follow the same path.

1263
01:28:20.763 --> 01:28:21.890
[Mom] Hmm.

1264
01:28:21.965 --> 01:28:26.561
Well, I have to admit I've often dreamed
about straying from the path myself.

1265
01:28:28.239 --> 01:28:32.676
All right, Shizuku, go ahead
and do what your heart tells you.

1266
01:28:32.744 --> 01:28:36.943
But it's never easy when you do
things differently from everyone else.

1267
01:28:37.015 --> 01:28:41.953
If things don't go well,
you'll only have yourself to blame.

1268
01:28:42.021 --> 01:28:45.184
And I want you to eat meals with us,
no matter how busy you get.

1269
01:28:45.258 --> 01:28:47.726
That's right.
We like to see you once in a while.

1270
01:28:47.794 --> 01:28:50.525
- OK.
- Tell your sister we're finished.

1271
01:28:53.467 --> 01:28:55.459
I'll make us some tea.

1272
01:28:58.073 --> 01:29:00.598
[Shiho] Hey, Shizuku.

1273
01:29:00.675 --> 01:29:02.541
Dad let you have your own way,

1274
01:29:02.612 --> 01:29:05.513
but he wants you to study
and get into a good high school.

1275
01:29:05.581 --> 01:29:08.517
I know that.
It was written all over his face.

1276
01:29:08.585 --> 01:29:12.487
By the way,
I'm gonna be moving out next Sunday.

1277
01:29:12.556 --> 01:29:14.525
You'll have the room to yourself.

1278
01:29:14.592 --> 01:29:16.958
You're moving out? I didn't know that.

1279
01:29:17.028 --> 01:29:19.588
[Shiho] Yep.
You're gonna be on your own now.

1280
01:29:27.273 --> 01:29:29.708
[Panting]

1281
01:29:29.776 --> 01:29:34.714
[Baron] Hurry! Faster! Faster!

1282
01:29:34.782 --> 01:29:37.717
Only one stone is genuine.

1283
01:29:37.785 --> 01:29:39.980
Which one? Which one is real?

1284
01:29:40.054 --> 01:29:41.920
[Baron] You are on your own now.

1285
01:29:41.990 --> 01:29:45.187
You must make the choice yourself.

1286
01:29:45.260 --> 01:29:46.591
Hurry!

1287
01:29:48.264 --> 01:29:49.595
[Gasping]

1288
01:30:03.348 --> 01:30:05.475
[Shizuku screaming]

1289
01:30:38.054 --> 01:30:39.385
[Blowing]

1290
01:31:00.648 --> 01:31:02.912
[Snoring]

1291
01:31:07.689 --> 01:31:10.214
[Creaking]

1292
01:31:23.206 --> 01:31:26.176
Louise, you've come back to me.

1293
01:31:26.244 --> 01:31:30.510
I'm sorry I've grown old.
I didn't know you'd return.

1294
01:31:35.054 --> 01:31:36.646
[Thump]

1295
01:31:40.994 --> 01:31:44.395
[Sighing]

1296
01:31:45.598 --> 01:31:47.863
[Creaking]

1297
01:31:55.444 --> 01:31:58.607
Shizuku. Please, come on in.

1298
01:31:58.680 --> 01:32:02.378
I was just taking a nap.

1299
01:32:02.452 --> 01:32:04.886
Did I wake you? I'm sorry.

1300
01:32:04.954 --> 01:32:08.152
I hate to bother you, Mr. Nishi,
but my story's finished.

1301
01:32:09.827 --> 01:32:12.227
Ooh, wonderful.

1302
01:32:12.296 --> 01:32:14.765
Oh, you should be very proud.

1303
01:32:15.867 --> 01:32:19.599
Well, here it is. You're the first one
to read it, just as promised.

1304
01:32:19.672 --> 01:32:21.537
Well, this is a good-sized novel.

1305
01:32:21.607 --> 01:32:25.099
Whisper of the Heart
by Shizuku Tsukishima.

1306
01:32:25.177 --> 01:32:27.976
I know it's a bit long,
but could you read it right away?

1307
01:32:28.048 --> 01:32:30.107
I'll just wait here, if you don't mind.

1308
01:32:30.183 --> 01:32:33.119
I could, but you've
put so much into this.

1309
01:32:33.187 --> 01:32:35.621
Shouldn't I take my time
and read it carefully?

1310
01:32:35.690 --> 01:32:38.454
I'd rather you read it now,
'cause I'm kind of nervous.

1311
01:32:38.526 --> 01:32:41.257
You don't have to read it all,
just a few pages.

1312
01:32:41.330 --> 01:32:44.857
And then...
then if it's boring you can quit.

1313
01:32:44.933 --> 01:32:47.596
I understand. I'll read it right away.

1314
01:32:47.670 --> 01:32:51.128
Have a seat by the fire.
It's getting cold.

1315
01:32:55.846 --> 01:32:59.214
There. Now no one will disturb us.

1316
01:33:02.888 --> 01:33:06.290
Uh, would it be OK with you
if I wait downstairs?

1317
01:33:06.359 --> 01:33:07.986
- Hmm?
- I won't get cold.

1318
01:33:08.061 --> 01:33:09.585
I'd rather not watch you read.

1319
01:33:11.431 --> 01:33:15.095
Hmm. That'll be fine. Go ahead.

1320
01:34:09.131 --> 01:34:12.124
[Jets roaring]

1321
01:34:20.577 --> 01:34:22.772
[Door opening]

1322
01:34:27.852 --> 01:34:29.843
So, there you are.

1323
01:34:29.921 --> 01:34:32.482
I finished your book, Shizuku.

1324
01:34:34.160 --> 01:34:37.095
Thank you, dear.
It was really wonderful.

1325
01:34:37.163 --> 01:34:38.791
No, it's not! It's a mess.

1326
01:34:38.865 --> 01:34:40.833
The storyline goes all over the place.

1327
01:34:40.901 --> 01:34:43.165
All the characters' dialogue
sounds corny.

1328
01:34:43.236 --> 01:34:46.365
You have to tell me the truth.
I know it's a complete disaster.

1329
01:34:46.440 --> 01:34:50.673
No. It's just a bit rough, dear,
like Seiji's violin.

1330
01:34:50.746 --> 01:34:53.044
What I read was raw and heartfelt.

1331
01:34:55.317 --> 01:34:57.752
You should be very proud
for all your hard work.

1332
01:34:57.820 --> 01:35:01.256
You've dug inside your soul
and found some real gems.

1333
01:35:01.324 --> 01:35:05.284
Next you'll need to polish it,
which will also take a lot of work.

1334
01:35:06.964 --> 01:35:11.095
There's no need to be upset.
Just have a little patience.

1335
01:35:11.169 --> 01:35:13.899
[Sobbing]

1336
01:35:35.797 --> 01:35:39.131
Now let's go inside. It's cold out here.

1337
01:35:39.201 --> 01:35:40.930
OK. [sniffling]

1338
01:35:41.003 --> 01:35:44.405
I'm sorry. I know I shouldn't be crying.

1339
01:35:44.474 --> 01:35:47.204
I wanted so badly to do a good job,

1340
01:35:47.277 --> 01:35:51.009
but there's so much that I don't know
about writing. [sobbing]

1341
01:35:51.082 --> 01:35:55.576
And Seiji, he's so much
more accomplished than I am.

1342
01:35:55.653 --> 01:35:58.145
[Sniffling] I can never catch up.

1343
01:35:58.223 --> 01:36:00.487
I can never be good enough.

1344
01:36:00.559 --> 01:36:02.550
[Crying]

1345
01:36:02.628 --> 01:36:05.757
I see. You must be very fond of Seiji.

1346
01:36:09.970 --> 01:36:11.961
[Shizuku slurping]

1347
01:36:19.514 --> 01:36:21.573
[Sniffling]

1348
01:36:22.717 --> 01:36:24.743
[Blowing]

1349
01:36:25.921 --> 01:36:27.855
How do you like your noodles, hmm?

1350
01:36:27.923 --> 01:36:30.586
[Sniffling] I like them a lot.

1351
01:36:32.062 --> 01:36:34.860
When Seiji finished making
his very first violin,

1352
01:36:34.931 --> 01:36:37.492
he was far more upset
than you are today.

1353
01:36:37.568 --> 01:36:41.299
It took four batches of noodles
to calm him down. [chuckling]

1354
01:36:44.209 --> 01:36:46.404
Ah. Thank you, dear.

1355
01:36:47.680 --> 01:36:50.741
Now tell me, how far did we get
into the Baron's story?

1356
01:36:50.817 --> 01:36:54.412
You were a student in Germany
when you found the Baron in a cafe.

1357
01:36:54.487 --> 01:36:56.285
Ah, that's right.

1358
01:36:57.625 --> 01:37:02.085
I was captivated by his expression.
It was so sad and mysterious.

1359
01:37:02.163 --> 01:37:05.531
So I begged the owner of the cafe
to let me buy the Baron.

1360
01:37:05.600 --> 01:37:08.967
[Nishi] But he refused to sell it to me.

1361
01:37:09.038 --> 01:37:13.532
He said the Baron had a female companion
who was away for repairs.

1362
01:37:13.609 --> 01:37:15.805
The two of them made
such a beautiful couple

1363
01:37:15.879 --> 01:37:18.211
he didn't think it was right
to separate them.

1364
01:37:18.282 --> 01:37:23.186
I told him that as soon as the Baroness
was repaired, I'd buy them both.

1365
01:37:23.254 --> 01:37:26.781
The Baroness, her name
was Louise, isn't that right?

1366
01:37:26.858 --> 01:37:30.056
No one knows this,
but Louise was the name

1367
01:37:30.129 --> 01:37:32.620
of a woman I went to school with.

1368
01:37:32.698 --> 01:37:34.723
She and I became very close,

1369
01:37:34.800 --> 01:37:38.828
and every day we'd meet at the cafe
to see if the Baroness had returned.

1370
01:37:39.606 --> 01:37:43.134
Louise pleaded with the cafe owner
to sell me the Baron.

1371
01:37:43.211 --> 01:37:46.078
She promised to buy the Baroness
and hold onto her

1372
01:37:46.147 --> 01:37:48.810
until the two statues could be reunited.

1373
01:37:48.884 --> 01:37:51.614
Finally the cafe owner agreed,

1374
01:37:51.687 --> 01:37:54.053
and I left for Japan with the Baron.

1375
01:37:54.123 --> 01:37:58.561
I promised Louise that I would return
to Germany as soon as possible,

1376
01:37:58.628 --> 01:38:02.963
and I vowed that when the Baron
and Baroness were reunited,

1377
01:38:03.033 --> 01:38:04.694
so would we be.

1378
01:38:07.705 --> 01:38:10.436
But the war began
soon after my departure

1379
01:38:10.509 --> 01:38:14.639
and I wasn't able to return to Germany
until many years later.

1380
01:38:16.849 --> 01:38:19.784
I visited our cafe and I searched
all over Germany

1381
01:38:19.852 --> 01:38:21.844
but I could find no trace of her.

1382
01:38:23.624 --> 01:38:27.321
I never saw Louise
or the Baroness again.

1383
01:38:29.063 --> 01:38:32.794
I'm sorry. So that's why you never
want to talk about the Baron.

1384
01:38:32.867 --> 01:38:35.996
But you've done something
wonderful for me, Shizuku.

1385
01:38:36.071 --> 01:38:40.269
What was only a memory for me has
gained new life thanks to your story.

1386
01:38:40.342 --> 01:38:42.334
Oh, that reminds me.

1387
01:38:50.021 --> 01:38:52.421
Now hold out your hands.

1388
01:38:58.363 --> 01:38:59.557
But I...

1389
01:38:59.631 --> 01:39:02.499
That geode suits you better than me.

1390
01:39:02.569 --> 01:39:04.093
I want you to have it.

1391
01:39:05.305 --> 01:39:08.434
Promise me you'll polish
your story well.

1392
01:39:08.509 --> 01:39:11.444
I will. [sniffling]

1393
01:39:24.727 --> 01:39:26.592
Thanks for everything, Mr. Nishi.

1394
01:39:26.662 --> 01:39:28.187
My pleasure.

1395
01:39:30.868 --> 01:39:32.597
See you later.

1396
01:39:40.846 --> 01:39:42.837
[Door opening]

1397
01:39:42.915 --> 01:39:45.315
- [Shizuku] Anyone home?
- I'm in here.

1398
01:39:48.021 --> 01:39:49.818
Is Dad around?

1399
01:39:49.890 --> 01:39:51.221
He's in the bathtub.

1400
01:39:51.291 --> 01:39:53.486
Do you know what time it is,
young lady?

1401
01:39:53.560 --> 01:39:55.552
I'd like to make a formal announcement.

1402
01:39:55.630 --> 01:39:57.996
I've decided that I want
to attend high school.

1403
01:39:58.065 --> 01:40:00.260
- I'll start studying tomorrow.
- Really?

1404
01:40:00.334 --> 01:40:03.133
Does that mean you've already
finished your project?

1405
01:40:03.205 --> 01:40:04.866
For the time being.

1406
01:40:06.108 --> 01:40:08.577
Do you want dinner? I made curry.

1407
01:40:08.645 --> 01:40:10.636
[Shizuku] No, thanks.

1408
01:40:10.713 --> 01:40:13.307
[Sighing] For the time being, huh?

1409
01:40:13.383 --> 01:40:15.375
[Chuckling]

1410
01:40:20.392 --> 01:40:22.826
[Sighing]

1411
01:40:22.894 --> 01:40:25.658
[Dad] Shizuku, the bathroom's free
if you want it.

1412
01:40:31.871 --> 01:40:35.603
[Deep breathing]

1413
01:40:45.153 --> 01:40:47.816
Look at her, my little warrior.

1414
01:40:50.359 --> 01:40:51.951
Let's see.

1415
01:40:58.568 --> 01:41:00.298
[Dad] Sweet dreams.

1416
01:41:01.105 --> 01:41:02.766
[Closing door]

1417
01:41:16.723 --> 01:41:18.384
Huh?

1418
01:41:38.814 --> 01:41:40.476
[Sighing]

1419
01:41:41.218 --> 01:41:42.685
[Shuddering]

1420
01:41:54.700 --> 01:41:56.031
Seiji?

1421
01:42:03.443 --> 01:42:05.434
Yeah. Just a second.

1422
01:42:06.280 --> 01:42:09.010
[Rattling]

1423
01:42:20.196 --> 01:42:22.721
I can't believe this.
You were actually awake.

1424
01:42:22.799 --> 01:42:24.323
This isn't a dream, is it?

1425
01:42:24.400 --> 01:42:27.893
No. I came back from Italy
a day early. Get on.

1426
01:42:27.971 --> 01:42:29.802
Oh, wait a minute.

1427
01:42:29.873 --> 01:42:31.670
You'll be cold like that.

1428
01:42:34.079 --> 01:42:36.138
OK, hop on.

1429
01:42:36.214 --> 01:42:40.208
- You'll be cold. I'll get a jacket.
- There's not enough time. Let's go.

1430
01:42:42.154 --> 01:42:44.145
All right, hold on tight now.

1431
01:42:49.629 --> 01:42:51.996
[Seiji] I wanted to see you
as soon as I got home,

1432
01:42:52.066 --> 01:42:55.558
so I stood outside your window
hoping you'd look outside and see me.

1433
01:42:55.636 --> 01:42:58.868
Suddenly you were standing there.
I couldn't believe my eyes.

1434
01:42:58.941 --> 01:43:01.102
We must be meant
for each other, Shizuku.

1435
01:43:01.176 --> 01:43:03.235
I still can't believe I'm not dreaming.

1436
01:43:03.312 --> 01:43:05.577
Who cares? This is a great dream.

1437
01:43:05.648 --> 01:43:07.240
[Horn beeping]

1438
01:43:10.653 --> 01:43:12.519
How did things go in Italy?

1439
01:43:12.590 --> 01:43:15.388
[Seiji] My master said
I'm not great yet, but I could be.

1440
01:43:15.459 --> 01:43:17.586
I've decided to finish
high school first,

1441
01:43:17.661 --> 01:43:19.186
then I'll go back to Cremona.

1442
01:43:27.874 --> 01:43:30.206
- Should I get off?
- No. Stay on.

1443
01:43:30.276 --> 01:43:34.680
I decided I was going
to ride up this steep hill

1444
01:43:34.748 --> 01:43:36.613
carrying you with me. [panting]

1445
01:43:36.683 --> 01:43:38.345
Who said you could decide that?

1446
01:43:38.419 --> 01:43:40.546
[Panting]

1447
01:43:40.622 --> 01:43:43.022
I don't want to be
just a burden for you.

1448
01:43:45.961 --> 01:43:49.988
If I'm going with you
I'm going to help you.

1449
01:43:50.065 --> 01:43:53.331
[Panting] All right, go ahead and help.

1450
01:43:53.403 --> 01:43:54.995
Just a bit further.

1451
01:43:55.071 --> 01:43:57.802
[Both panting]

1452
01:44:08.887 --> 01:44:11.948
Shizuku, hurry up! Get on!

1453
01:44:24.940 --> 01:44:27.738
[Panting]

1454
01:44:29.878 --> 01:44:31.938
Ah, just in time.

1455
01:44:33.216 --> 01:44:34.740
Wow.

1456
01:44:36.819 --> 01:44:38.811
- Need a hand?
- I'm fine.

1457
01:44:42.025 --> 01:44:43.424
Look at this.

1458
01:44:59.980 --> 01:45:01.641
Amazing.

1459
01:45:01.715 --> 01:45:04.116
With all that mist,
it looks like the ocean.

1460
01:45:04.185 --> 01:45:06.653
Yeah. This is where I come
to get inspired.

1461
01:45:06.721 --> 01:45:08.450
You'll see in a second.

1462
01:45:52.974 --> 01:45:55.033
[Seiji] I wanted to show this to you.

1463
01:45:55.109 --> 01:45:56.634
It's beautiful, isn't it?

1464
01:45:58.047 --> 01:46:01.710
Grandpa told me about all
the amazing writing you've been doing.

1465
01:46:01.784 --> 01:46:04.185
I feel bad that I wasn't here
to encourage you.

1466
01:46:04.254 --> 01:46:06.119
I was just off thinking about myself.

1467
01:46:06.189 --> 01:46:09.386
Mm-mmm. You're the one
who inspired me, Seiji.

1468
01:46:09.459 --> 01:46:11.519
I'm glad I pushed myself.

1469
01:46:11.595 --> 01:46:13.654
I know myself a little bit better now.

1470
01:46:15.566 --> 01:46:17.933
I realized I need a lot more schooling,

1471
01:46:18.003 --> 01:46:21.336
so I don't mind doing what it takes
to get into a good high school.

1472
01:46:21.406 --> 01:46:24.501
Shizuku. I've been thinking.

1473
01:46:24.577 --> 01:46:26.067
It's that...

1474
01:46:26.145 --> 01:46:28.875
I know this might sound
really weird to you,

1475
01:46:28.948 --> 01:46:31.315
but could you see us
getting married someday?

1476
01:46:31.385 --> 01:46:32.750
[Gasping]

1477
01:46:32.820 --> 01:46:35.345
I promise I'll be
a professional violin maker

1478
01:46:35.422 --> 01:46:37.618
and you can be a professional writer.

1479
01:46:39.627 --> 01:46:41.322
Mm-hmm.

1480
01:46:41.396 --> 01:46:43.558
Does this sound corny?

1481
01:46:43.632 --> 01:46:46.760
It's a little corny, but you're
a violin maker, not a writer.

1482
01:46:46.836 --> 01:46:48.895
That's true. This is great!

1483
01:46:48.971 --> 01:46:52.703
Come here. It's getting cold.

1484
01:46:52.776 --> 01:46:55.871
Shizuku, I love you!

